{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/437815-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-7","id":437815,"title":"Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga (Actual Play) Part 7","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-11T18:24:44-07:00","id":437815,"title":"Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga (Actual Play) Part 7","content":"The Kiddie Pool Saga Continues!<br /> <br /> Previous Chapters and Character Portraits can be found here [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\">LINK</a>]<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Back Story</u></b><br /> <br /> In part four of the write up (links in my sig), I wrote about how Michael Seville had asked Susan Small to speak with his childe, Kurt Hoffman about the Ordo Dracul. Since then, Kurt has become a slave of the Ordo Dracul and Susan has acted as his mentor in the coils. I once asked Susan for how long she intended to keep teaching Kurt. She responded thusly:<br /> <br /> <b>Susan Small:</b> &quot;I will teach him as much as I can for as long as I can. It's not often that Michel Seville asks for boons that are not already owed to him.&quot;<br /> <br /> As part of this agreement, Seville will provide security for Susan when she travels into the Quarantine Zone or Kiddie Pool to teach Kurt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>More Back Story</u></b><br /> <br /> When the Quarantine Zone was being set up, Michael Seville made a back channel deal with the newest member of the Primogen Council (Septimus) to make the newly formed Quarantine Zone the domain of Michael Seville. As Alice and I were hounds at the time, we were quite influential in the creation of the Quarantine Experience.<br /> <br /> 1. The storage garages where the new vampires make their havens? Our idea.<br /> 2. The butcher shop that Cooper runs to feed the little ingrates? Our idea.<br /> <br /> Well Michael Seville is a Carthian, so he was quite interested to hear our ideas on vampire government. Anyway, contrary to popular belief, the Quarantine Zone is not contestable land. It is Seville's land, which means that feeding there without permission is poaching. Seville wanted to hear our ideas how to award feeding rights amongst the newcomers. Here is what we came up with:<br /> <br /> 3. The tickets. Each night, Cooper will distribute a limited number of tickets which are good for one feeding within the Quarantine Zone. If you don't have a ticket, I guess you're stuck drinking cold blood from Cooper's butcher shop. The color of the tickets changes every few weeks, and the number of tickets released changes from night to night (to avoid overfeeding in the area.)<br /> <br /> This system isn't permanent. In Michael Seville's words, he plans to &quot;shake things up&quot; from time to time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Still More Back Story</u></b><br /> <br /> When I looked at Eve's ledger and discovered that Theodore had a transferable boon from Aika and Aiko. Eve Mentioned at the time that she knew a secret about Theodore that if we knew it would allow us to &quot;own him.&quot; We declined at that time. We have accrued over time lots of little boon debts here and there. We are trying to become creditors as opposed to debtors now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Caged Heat</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I had recently been awarded the lives and freedom of Aika and Aiko (daeva twins, lancea sanctum.) As it turns out, Aika and Aiko didn't feel the same way Alice and I did about the situation. We tracked them to the northeast side of the city, which is now fallow territory but was formerly occupied by &quot;the Boss.&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a bus station in that territory with nightly departures. To make a long story short, Alice and I were able to track them down. There was some fighting, and we were able to stake them and take them. They were fed animal blood from Cooper's butcher shop through a funnel to prevent torpor/heal damage/prevent immediate hunger frenzy.<br /> <br /> Anyway, when we pulled the stakes from their hearts they woke up in bird cages which I have described last chapter. We spent about a month doing psychological torture, feeding them our blood, and applying Dominate powers to them. You know, wholesome family activities.<br /> <br /> Out of character, Felix has a Dominate devotion called &quot;the Stepford Devotion.&quot; It is similar to Conditioning, which is a prerequisite. However, rather than creating drooling servants with no personal initiative, the Stepford Devotion is used to make permanent changes to the victim's personality. It can be subtle and minor, or enact more drastic changes in the thoughts, beliefs, and behaviors of the victim. Aika is now blood bound to Alice, and Aiko to me. They were both purchased as five dot retainers. So, evil dominate powers, blood bonds, and experience points have transformed Aika and Aiko into loyal retainers who serve House Fox.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Terry's First Meeting</u></b><br /> <br /> I had been wondering about Terry's status in the city. Last chapter, she participated in an action of the Mekhetocracy. This would usually indicate that a Mekhet had become a citizen, but I prefer not to speculate.<br /> <br /> The most recent meeting of the Mekhetocracy took place in the steamy bath downtown where many such meetings are held. As usual, we disrobe and enter the pool, which is heated to a pleasant bathwater temperature. Terry arrives last, sheepishly holding her robe to cover her modesty.<br /> <br /> <b>Kyle</b> looks at Terry and quotes her poem: &quot;So join our ranks and go through the Rite, We always need kindred willing to fight.&quot;<br /> <b>Terry:</b> &quot;Stop that. Don't make fun of me.&quot;<br /> <b>Kyle:</b> &quot;I'm not making fun of you.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;Your poem is awesome Terry.&quot;<br /> <b>Alice:</b> &quot;We loved it.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Prince enters the room. We do not recognize him by face, but his potent beast is unmistakable. Tonight, he appears as a statue of Apollo. His skin is of white marble and muscled perfection with hair of gold. At that time, I feel the Prince using some kind of Auspex devotion which extended the Prince's power of aura perception to everyone present. The storyteller described it as being soaked in the rain. I looked around the room and watched the auras of all present respond as the Prince quoted the same verse from Terry's poem that Kyle just had. And in that moment, I finally realized what the Mekhetocracy is. It is a cult. It is the cult of the Prince.<br /> <br /> <b>The Prince:</b> &quot;They aren't lying to you Terry. This is your city. Welcome home.&quot;<br /> <br /> Terry looked around the room at all of us, dropped her robe, and joined us in the pool. So yeah, I'm pretty sure Terry is a citizen now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Reeve</u></b><br /> <br /> After the death of Elliot Rex (nosferatu ancilla carthian sheriff) at the hands of his own childe Elliot Jr (nosferatu neonate carthian, my nemesis? really??) The office of the sheriff remained vacant for months. Eventually, after some influence peddling my cousin Antony (adopted childe of Octavia) was named sheriff. Soon after, three members of the Primogen Council (Appolonia, Pilgrim, and Septimus) voted in favor of greater autonomy for landowners in Baltimore. The Prince did not oppose them. Peter (seneschal, mekhet) responded by doing away with the office of the Sheriff and replacing it with that of Reeve. Reeve in Baltimore is basically the same as sheriff, but only Invictus are eligible to serve.<br /> <br /> Antony continues to serve the city, now as Reeve. His jurisdiction has shrunk considerably, and does not extend beyond the inner harbor (kiddie pool) and Locust Point. The rest of the city would be policed by Bailiffs, who would be appointed by individual landowners. To date, no Bailiffs have been named.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the mood in Elysium is that the Reeve is not doing a good job. Citizens do not feel safe traveling to Locust Point or the Inner Harbor. One of the Harpies (Melissa Hopps, crone, childe of the Keeper) has been spreading this view.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Terry (the Mekhet)</u></b><br /> <br /> So, on a typical night Alice and I had just returned from slaking our thirst on the campus of the University of Maryland (dragon territory.) We were heading home to check in when we noticed Terry running down the street, apparently in chase. Terry's service to her landlord (Antony) is to watch for poachers in his territory, and she takes her job seriously.<br /> <br /> Well, Alice and I decide to give chase as well. At first we are chasing Terry, but soon we see what she is chasing and we pull ahead. Terry is chasing a bird; some kind of hawk which happens to come equipped with a vampire's predatory aura. The bird in question was lowering itself for a landing and it appears to be traveling in the direction of Antony's bar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Standoff</u></b><br /> <br /> Antony's bar is not open to the public. In fact, if you were to walk past, you probably would be unaware there was a bar there at all. To access the bar, one must walk in a side door, down a flight of stairs, and down a hallway before encountering the bar's entrance. When we arrive inside, Sarah (gangrel, quarantine zone resident) is standing in the middle of the bar. The door to Antony's office is closed and some of his ghouls have guns trained on Sarah.<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;Hello Sarah, what's on your mind?&quot;<br /> <br /> Antony hears Alice's and my arrival, and decides to open his office and join us.<br /> <br /> <b>Sarah:</b> &quot;One of your family members is going to die this night. I overheard Theodore talking to some vampires. He said, 'the ventrue bitch will be at the speakeasy giving her lessons tonight. If you want to get her, tonight might be your only chance.'&quot;<br /> <br /> Alice and I immediately begin running. The road which hugs the inner harbor and leads to the speakeasy is often clogged with slow moving traffic and drunken pedestrians. So, rather than taking our car we run the whole way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Bigger Standoff</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I arrived at the speakeasy (the unofficial elysium of the kiddie pool) to find nothing obviously amiss. We enter through the backdoor and take the stairs up. On the third floor is the small hidden speakeasy which Alice and I had refurbished so long ago. On the second, there is a sound recording studio, and some kind of lounge with tables. There is a small room outside the recording booth.<br /> <br /> In the small room there are four vampires and two ghouls I do not recognize, and Sam Bast (nosferatu, carthian, one of Seville's men.) Sam is blocking the door to the recording booth.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire:</b> &quot;There are six of us, and one of you. So why don't you just stand aside and live to fight another day. &quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Sam Bast:</b> &quot;I'm Sorry I can't do that.&quot;<br /> <br /> I become visible, Alice does not (she does this often.)<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;I think you have miscalculated. You may have us outnumbered today, and you may even kill us. But this is Baltimore. You will be found, and you will be shown the light of day. You are all dead already, you just don't know it.&quot;<br /> <br /> The lead vampire turns and is about to say something, when another vampire who heretofore was cloaked by obfuscate makes himself known. In the corner of the room sits Michael Seville. He uncrosses his legs and folds the newspaper he had been reading.<br /> <br /> <b>Michael Seville:</b> &quot;Well that's enough of that.&quot; He took a drag from an imaginary cigarette and flicks it at the vampire leader.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Terrifying Violence</u></b><br /> <br /> The atmosphere in the room becomes very... dreadful. Alice and I block the exit as the invading vampires attempt to flee. We watch as one of them starts screaming that he is on fire and tears chunks from his flesh in an attempt to extinguish himself. As he casts aside chunks of himself and those chunks hit other vampires in the room, they also begin screaming and tearing at their own flesh. Seville has used his elder level dice pools and nightmare powers to wicked effect.<br /> <br /> Even though Alice and I were not targeted by the discipline, we were still operating at -7 dice pools due to the aura of dread in the area. After 3 rounds of holding the door, Alice and I fled downstairs to escape the terror. There, we intercepted the ghoul who was working the door and advised him not to rush upstairs. Soon after, the six vampires came limping down the stairs still pulling flesh from their bodies and flung themselves over the side of the pier into the bay below.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Aristocrats!</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I got our shit together and went back upstairs. The waiting room was covered in blood and viscera. Then, the door to the (sound proof) booth opened and Susan Small and Kurt Hoffman entered the room. We waved. &quot;Hiya Susan <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />&quot; She had difficulty maintaining her composure. Michael Seville was no longer present (or visible), but Sam Bast was.<br /> <br /> At about this time, Antony and Terry arrived (they drove.) We gave them a brief synopsis of the action and it was decided that Alice, Sam, and Kurt would escort Susan back to Konrad Von Berg's estate. Antoni and I would pursue the attackers.<br /> <br /> Well, it didn't take Sherlock Holmes to deduce that perhaps the intruders were heading towards their cars. So, we traveled to the nearby underground carpark. The intruders were there in various states of injury getting ready to enter their car. Antony and I wasted little time in bringing violence to the evil bastards. We violate city law by sending them immediately to torpor, save one for questioning. (the sheriff acted in defense of the city. We are in little danger of prosecution)<br /> <br /> All four of the vampires and two ghouls are put to death by the garden shears of the Archon Helen (mekhet, crone) but not before I ask them wtf they are doing and why. Truth is compelled with dominate, and the lucid one tells us they were there to kidnap the dragon girl and bring her to their boss, a guy named Elliot. We take a time out, and I sketch a portrait of Elliot Jr and show it to the guy. &quot;Yeah, that's him. Except he's bald now.&quot; Famous last words.<br /> <br /> We later learned that Spider and Jerome James (both nosferatu) usually would have been present with Sam Bast to guard Susan, but had other obligations that night. Seville was present (obviously), but Sam was unaware. So why was Sam so brave in the face of long odds? As it turns out, Sam is more afraid of Michael Seville than he is of this random gang of vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Family Meeting</u></b><br /> <br /> There was a family meeting scheduled for later in the week, but I considered this revelation reason enough to call for the family to meet immediately. The family gathered and there was some disappointed grumbling that the usual banquet was not present. (Usually my grandsire provides food and wine which is just as nourishing as blood at these gatherings, but it can't be prepared on the spur of the moment.) The following topics were discussed:<br /> <br /> 1. I recounted the events of the attack on Susan and informed my family of my belief that Elliot Jr has returned to town. It is agreed that the situation should be dealt with. Until Elliot Jr can be located we have all agreed to increase our personal security.<br /> <br /> 2. I ask my Grandsire about his relationship with Michael Seville. It is my current belief that the city government as we know it came about due to the long ago actions of an alliance/coterie of vampires which included my Grandsire, Michael Seville, and the Prince. Konrad is not feeling too talkative tonight. &quot;We are not enemies.&quot; Is all I can get out of him.<br /> <br /> 3. Octavia speaks more about Seville: &quot;Alder Seville seems to have great territorial ambitions of late. I fear he is preparing a political ambush.&quot;<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Septimus</b>: &quot;When the Prince chooses to step aside, I plan to climb to that lofty position.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;Why?&quot;<br /> <b>Septimus:</b> &quot;Because Konrad won't do it.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix: </b>&quot;I know that. I mean, why you? Why do you want to sit on the throne? You are not so powerful as to rule independently. Why would you make yourself and our family beholden to the church? Why not consider Peter as the next Prince. He is Invictus, he is older than you, and he has already been serving as Seneschal for a long time. If you press the issue, it may result in a civil war.&quot;<br /> <b>Septimus</b>: &quot;Peter is not that much older than me, and besides, Peter has a weakness: He will do what is best for the city. He will stand aside rather than let it come to civil war.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix</b>: &quot;You think that's a weakness? Interesting. Well, would it be the worst thing if Michael Seville became Prince? There are other elders up and down the east coast who may come here with avarice in their hearts. Only a powerful elder will scare them away. You are not that person, but Seville could be.&quot;<br /> <b>Septimus:</b> &quot;A Carthian? Are you crazy? If Michael Seville became Prince, so many of the priviledges you enjoy would fade away. The best territories which are currently held by Invictus, many by our family, would be chipped away and redistributed until we were pushed to the margins.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;But we would survive to grow our power for the next generation rather than invaded by foreign powers.&quot;<br /> <b>Septimus:</b> &quot;This is just typical. When I am acting in the family's interests everyone is so thankful. Thank you Septimus for helping me gain territory. Thank you Septimus for keeping the city free of other Ventrue. But, when I want something for myself it's &quot;Septimus, you shouldn't have joined the Primogen Council. Septimus, your reach exceeds your grasp.&quot;<br /> <b>Alice:</b> &quot;Septimus, you have recently acquired a lofty title, and it is a well deserved one. However, I believe that I have the best solution for the future of the city: Octavia should marry Peter. Peter should succeed the throne and Octavia should rule by his side. Invictus would remain dominant and our two families combined would be formidible.&quot;<br /> <br /> You gotta love Alice. She's a showstopper. There isn't much in the way of conversation after that little bomb got dropped.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>After the Meeting</u></b><br /> <br /> After the meeting, I asked for a private word with my Aunt and Uncle. In Septimus' office I tell him about a conversation I once had with Michael Seville. I tell him that Seville has a serious dislike and distrust of the church and will not allow the city to become a theocracy. I tell him to think about that as he makes his plans.<br /> <br /> Then, Susan enters the office unannounced dragging Christina by the arm.<br /> <br /> <b>Susan:</b> &quot;Tell them.&quot;<br /> <b>Christina:</b> &quot;I think I was being followed earlier tonight.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix</b> (getting a little angry): &quot;And you didn't think to mention that sooner? Christina... Alice and I cannot be everywhere at once. And while it is true that if you were taken we would risk our lives to save you, it would be much preferable if you would take your safety more seriously so Alice and I can focus on finding and destroying Elliot Jr and anyone else who thinks our family is weak.&quot;<br /> <b>Octavia:</b> &quot;Well, that settles it. Until this situation is resolved you are grounded to my estate unless you are accompanied by a heavy escort of some kind.&quot;<br /> <br /> Christina is not happy, but at least I will not have to worry about her for the time being. Susan, I know will be spending more time at home as she does in fact take her security seriously.<br /> <br /> That leaves Felicity, still a resident of the Kiddy Pool, for Alice and me to worry about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Diner's Club</u></b><br /> <br /> To ensure the safety of Felicity, we took the following steps.<br /> 1. Felicity, Kurt, and Nellie (her coterie) will move their haven to Locust Point near Antony, Alice and me.<br /> 2. The three of them will feed together and be accompanied when they do so. I order Aika and Aiko to accompany them on their dinner trips. I also order Patrick Brown (ordo dracul slave, nosferatu) to do so. It will take them a lot longer to get everyone fed, but six vampires some of whom are combat focused should dissuade any would be attackers.<br /> <br /> With the more vulnerable members of my family out of harm's way, Alice and I are now free to figure out what is going on and bring some justice to the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Questioning Theodore</u></b><br /> <br /> After the family meeting, Alice and I mentioned that we were going to go talk to Theodore (nosferatu.) Well, Susan wants to come with. So, the three of us arrive there with some extra ghouls early the next evening at the time when Cooper usually opens the butcher shop. Well, Theodore is not in a very talkative mood tonight.<br /> <br /> So, Susan walks into the butcher shop and asks if she could be the one to distribute the tickets tonight. Then, with a handful of tickets she walks across the parking lot to an old mechanic/oil change place. The locals have pulled a few couches and tables into there and use it as a night time hang out. Susan arrives and says &quot;Anyone who punches Theodore as hard as they can, gets a ticket.&quot; Then she throws the tickets in the air making it rain on the hungry neonates.<br /> <br /> Soon, several vampires swarm Theodore each taking their shot at him. Remember, the law states that you can only do so much damage to someone before you are on the wrong side of the law. By spreading the damage amongst several attackers, they are all in the clear, even though Theodore was on the receiving end of a proper beat down. Further, neither Alice, Susan, nor I have laid a finger on him.<br /> <br /> <b>Alice:</b> &quot;We will be back here every night until you talk... and we won't lay a finger on you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Theodore started talking. He told us that Jack's crew (the vampire leader from earlier this chapter) used to work for the Dark Lord (Joe, the Daeva whose entire bloodline we had destroyed), but there is a new player in Council territory. A new nosferatu who is getting crews to swear their fealty and work for him.<br /> <br /> Whether or not Theodore talked is irrelevant. He gave information to the group that tried to take Susan Small. Well, we went back to Eve Liebsch. We talked to her once more about her information about Theodore. She agrees to give it over to us in exchange for rights to make haven in our territory, which should be habitable in the not too distant future. She is not asking us to protect her haven or provide, only for the right to make it herself. We agree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Slow Motion Masquerade Breach</u></b><br /> <br /> Eve tells us that Theodore was involved in a bank heist. He broke into the home of a bank manager and took her and her son hostage. Well the bank robbery didn't go as planned and Theodore killed the woman and her child. Their bodies are in the trunk of a car which was dumped in a lake not too far out of town. Eve knows where the car is, and she knows that the car is registered to the mortal identity of Theodore. It is only a matter of time before the car is found and pulled from the lake.<br /> <br /> Alice and I take this information to Michael Seville. Theodore is never seen again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>And Speaking of the Masquerade...</u></b><br /> <br /> One night, we get a phone call from a mortal contact we have maintained since our days in the kiddie pool. When we met him he was a veterinarian who slept on a couch in his office which was above a pet store. The pet store in question was a frequently used feeding ground by neonates of the kiddy pool, and after being awakened in the night by screaming animals over and over the veterinarian figured out that monsters were real.<br /> <br /> Over time, we learned that the veterinarian was actually trained as a medical doctor, but due to financial issues was unable to get his medical degree and license. Alice and I pulled some strings at the university and the veterinarian became the assistant coroner.<br /> <br /> Anyway, one night we receive a phone call from the assistant coroner. He tells us that he really needs to see us tonight. Alice and I travel to the basement of the county hospital where we are privy to the following tableau:<br /> <br /> 1. The coroner's office is in disarray. Some of the tables are knocked over.<br /> 2. There are three dead humans on the floor; two security guards and one doctor.<br /> 3. There is another body on the floor in advanced stages of decomposition.<br /> 4. In the corner is the assistant coroner, also on the floor. He is holding his stomach, blood seeping through his fingers.<br /> <br /> The assistant coroner informs us that the police found a body in an airshaft of a downtown office building. They assumed that the body belonged to a thief who got stuck long ago and died in the airshaft. However, it turned out that the body was that of a torpid vampire. The vampire in question woke from torpor, frenzied, and killed the coroner and two security guards before the assistant coroner was able to draw his pistol and empty it into the vampire's head.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for us, the coroner's office is in a secluded part of the hospital basement. Unfortunately for us, shift change was in less than three hours. We had to act fast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Coverup</u></b><br /> <br /> It should come as no surprise that Alice and I took actions to maintain the masquerade. Here is what we did:<br /> <br /> 1. First, we moved the rapidly decaying corpse into a morgue drawer in case some hospital staff would arrive early or some such.<br /> 2. The coroner's wound is mortal, but the bleeding is slow. He has an hour or two to live (according to him. I'm not a doctor.)<br /> 3. We contacted Michael Seville and asked for permission to take a mortal from his territory to be made into a ghoul (the county hospital is in his territory.)<br /> 4. We had felicity (my sister) to the hospital and convinced her that the assistant coroner would make an excellent ghoul for her. She had not yet made a ghoul and had somehow gotten it into her head that her first ghoul should be a &quot;butler to run the household of other ghouls.&quot; We were able to convince her that an asset in the position of the coroner's office would be an opportunity for her to get boons. Other kindred would, from time to time need a favor from the coroner's office, after all.<br /> 5. The Assistant coroner is made a ghoul and healed.<br /> 6. We got our story straight. A junky broke in looking for narcotics, and when he didn't get what he wanted. He started hacking people to bits with a machete.<br /> 7. We mutilated the corpses with a machete and ransacked some of the medicine cabinets.<br /> 8. We removed the vampire body from the coroner's office and rented a boat to dump it in the bay.<br /> <br /> All this prep work is well and good, but we weren't finished yet. Once the assistant coroner gives his statement to the police there would be a manhunt. This is the sort of high profile crime that will get attention. There will be pressure from on high to solve it. We needed a patsy.<br /> <br /> We were sitting there, debating the ethics of pinning a crime on an innocent man and seeing him sentenced to jail or even put to death. Our first instinct was to find someone who deserved it; someone who perhaps had gotten away with murder previously. Then, Alice had a brilliant Idea.<br /> <br /> Alice: &quot;You know, Habsburg Day is coming up...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Habsburg Day</u></b><br /> <br /> A few chapters back, a mortal gang robbed an art dealer in downtown Baltimore. In the process of that robbery, they killed the parents of Tigger (former blood doll of Alice and Felix. Current ghoul of Terry the mekhet) and destroyed the Habsburg Lillies (and old and expensive work of art.) The Keeper of Elysium, Madeline Ross (invictus, ancilla) asked Alice and I to look into the matter. At the conclusion of our investigation Alice and I delared a new holiday, Habsburg Day. We told the keeper that every year on Habsburg Day, we would find one of the culprits and do something bad to them. Here is what we did:<br /> <br /> 1. We tracked down the gang in question.<br /> 2. We planted a bag full of vials of morphine and ketamine in the trunk of one of their cars.<br /> 3. We also planted the machete which was used to mutilate the corpses of the security guards and coroner in the same man's trunk.<br /> 4. We captured the patsy and used Dominate on him to change his memories and add some compulsions:<br /> a. He now has memories that make him believe he is in fact the murderer.<br /> b. He will think it's a great idea to sell the morphine and ketamine to make some extra cash.<br /> 5. We also used Dominate on his girlfriend. According to her, on the night of the murder he drove her home from a party and wanted to come inside for some nookie. She declined, because she saw a machete in the back seat and that made her nervous. (we chose this gang member for this Habsburg Day precisely because he did attend a party that night, and he did drop his girl friend off at home before going home himself and having no alibi for the time of thecrime.)<br /> 6. We contacted one of Octavia's ghouls, a cop. (we helped him with an internal affairs investigation a few chapters back.) We asked the cop to point one of the police departments in the direction of the gang member and send a confidential informant to do a drug buy.<br /> <br /> So, a confidential informant buys drugs from the guy which turn out to be morphine and ketamine in hospital vials. This leads to a search of the guy's home and car which turn up the murder weapon (machete with victims blood on it.) In the course of the investigation, the girlfriend tells the cops about seeing the machete on the night of the murders and being afraid of it. All this, combined with a lack of alibi makes this a slam dunk case.<br /> <br /> Happy Habsburg Day!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Next Week: The Foxes Face off with Elliot Jr!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:06:45-07:00","id":440090,"title":"","content":"I think Michael Seville is my favourite NPC. In some ways Seville seems like he'd make an ideal Prince of the city. On the other hand, his interests would likely oppose the Fox family's interests. It will be interesting to see how this particular dynamic plays out, particularly as ts likely a lot of the city owe Seville boons.<br /> <br /> As ever, am looking forward to reading more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T03:08:12-07:00","id":442386,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Seville's pretty cool. It's one of the things that worries Dorris Bettes so much about him. Not only does she think he would be a terrifying dictator, but a terrifying dictator who would win the hearts and minds of the people. Alice and I once had a conversation with Seville in which we asked him what the city would look like if he succeeded the throne. He didn't give us specifics, but did tell us, &quot;You would do well under my rule, and you would enjoy it.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for Dorris, she made a big mistake in the eyes of Felix. On the night when the Prince called for all the kindred in the city to fight, Dorris and her coterie showed up in Elysium wearing the light colors of a non-combatant. It is probable that Dorris didn't understand the importance of the night. It doesn't matter to me though. When the city called for her, she wasn't there. While she sat comfortably in Elysium, my fledgling little sister was fighting werewolves. Dorris will always be a second class citizen in my eyes.<br /> <br /> Further, Dorris is in a bit of a predicament. She has recently taken some discouraged actions. <br /> <br /> 1. Dorris went over to council territory and actively encouraged the massive immigration which has been causing Alice and me all kinds of headaches. It is her hope that the population of Carthians will grow in the city and that some among them will form a power bloc to act as a check to Michael Seville's status and power in the covenant.<br /> 2. Dorris took it upon herself to go telling the newcomers the laws of the city as evidenced by uppity neonates like Jonathan Poole petitioning multiple authorities for redress of grievances a few chapters back.<br /> <br /> Remember, there is a difference between discouraged and forbidden actions in the eyes of the law. Dorris isn't going to be dragged in front of the courts and punished. She hasn't broken the law. However, her actions are bothersome to the powers that be. It is the main reason that Seville allowed us to screw Dorris out of the best territory when homesteads were being given to neonate coteries. After all, why should he warn her of our subterfuge if she isn't going to behave like a good girl? Until she pulls her head out of her ass, she will not enjoy the benefits of cover that other kindred in good standing can expect from their elders and covenant leaders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T03:14:41-07:00","id":442390,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Tag</u></b><br /> <br /> One night Kyle (mekhet, neonate, childe of the archon Simon) approaches Alice and me. He tells us that one of the new Quarantine Zone residents has made a mistake. During a conversation with Terry (mekhet, carthian, newest citizen) he asked her, &quot;Who is the stupid bitch that made you a citizen?&quot; Well, the Prince made Terry a citizen. The Prince does not tolerate insults, regardless of how minor.<br /> <br /> So, the three of us along with Lucien Du Lac and Betty (all mekhet) travel to the quarantine zone under cloak of obfuscate. When mekhet travel together in this way, they use a technique called 'shallow cloak.' It is not a devotion. Basically, when establishing obfuscate the character will 'pull their punch' so to speak. In the event of a clash of wills, the character will discard all but one success making it easier for those with auspex to spot them while remaining invisible to those without.<br /> <br /> We arrive in the Quarantine Zone in search of Pip (the poor soul who unwittingly insulted the Prince.) We have come armed with screwdrivers and ice picks, because we intend to make the dood suffer. The rules of the game are simple: tag the target and pull back. Recloak when the target is distracted by the next attack. If he tags you, you lose. So, we catch Pip leaving the strip club called &quot;Private Eye&quot; which is one of the better, if seedier, feeding grounds in the Quarantine Zone. In the back alley behind the club we attack.<br /> <br /> Pip is sent to final death via a series of dozens of tiny puncture wounds. Sucks to be him. On the bright side, it isn't Alice and me who are tasked with dealing with the body. Woot!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Foreign Affairs</u></b><br /> <br /> So, we have realized that Elliot Jr. is back in town and has already attacked our family by proxy. We have further realized that he is operating out of Council territory to the south and west of the city. Before we saddle up and ride, we decide to have a conversation with Alice's sire, Mary Sue. It is Mary Sue's responsibility within the mekhetocracy to deal with foreign affairs and intel analysis.<br /> <br /> Mary Sue tells us that it would be inadvisable to go into council territory with our guns blazing. There are dozens of kindred who live there, and not all of them are pushovers. Further, she tells us that for a long time, there has been an absolute prohibition against creation of new kindred in council territory. That prohibition has recently been lifted (as evidenced by the recent flood of kindred in both council territory and the quarantine zone.) Finally, Mary Sue warns us against upsetting the balance of power in council territory. They have been fighting a simmering skirmish conflict with one of the two packs of werewolves whose territory abuts theirs.<br /> <br /> Well this changes the situation. Rushing into Elliot Jr's home field is not really an option. We will have to be patient and careful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Asylum Seeker</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I received a message from Abigail Taft. She wanted a meeting. We met her and her coterie in the Locust Point Industrial Zone, which was currently being developed into the territories of neonate coteries. Abigail's coterie consists of the following kindred:<br /> <br /> Abigail Taft (mekhet, carthian)<br /> Miles (daeva, carthian)<br /> Jonathan Poole (daeva, carthian)<br /> Angela (daeva, carthian)<br /> <br /> Abigail is worried about her safety and that of her coterie. She wants Alice and I to speak for her to the Reeve and gain permission for her and her compatriots to move across the bay from the Quarantine Zone into the Kiddie Pool. Well, we have some serious concerns about a few members of her coterie.<br /> <br /> 1. Jonathan Poole has a serious white night complex. He will come to the rescue of any woman, regardless of the facts or rationality of the situation.<br /> 2. Angela. The recent attack on our haven was nearly led by Angela. She was moments from crossing my threshold before Miles pulled her away and talked some sense into her. Even though she didn't go through with it, I still bear her a certain level of ill will. I hope you understand.<br /> <br /> Abigail is not one to give up so easily. She tells that there are dangerous vampires who are loyal to the Council who have arrived in the Quarantine Zone. She tells us that there is a gang of vampires led by Easy (spelled EZE.) Well, neither Alice nor I were particularly interested in expending boons to bring this group of Carthians across the bay. Further, we are not too keen on any of the former Council residents gaining citizenship in Baltimore. If the threats against Abigail and her friends are real and they are killed, Alice and I will have the excuse we need to bring final death to EZE and his crew. Win-Win, right?<br /> <br /> I begin by responding to her concerns with light hearted banter. I tell her that the city doesn't particularly need a white knight, to say nothing of Angela's shortcomings. Abigail assures me that she is getting Jonathan under control.<br /> <br /> <b>Abigail:</b> &quot;His psychosexual development is stuck in the teenage white knight phase. I'm working on it.&quot;<br /> <br /> What follows are Dominatrix jokes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Asylum Seeker (redux)</u></b><br /> <br /> A few nights later Alice and I are walking from our haven toward the bridge which leads to the Quarantine Zone. On our way, we see a vampire who is limp/jogging toward the lights of Locust Point. He is looking around in a panic. I decide to find out what's up. I approach him and ask what's going on. &quot;They're going to kill me! You gotta help me. I need to see the local lord.&quot; He points toward the lights of Locust Point. I lead him there, but steer him toward Alice's and my croft.<br /> <br /> I lead him to a rooftop where we can speak more privately and inform him that he is speaking to the one he seeks. He begs for asylum, and we are soon joined by three other vampires:<br /> <br /> Sam Bast (nosferatu, carthian)<br /> Spider (nosferatu, future invictus)<br /> Jerome James (nosferatu, carthian)<br /> <br /> Sam begins laying out a tarp on the roof while Spider and Jerome flank the guy. I begin speaking in Latin.<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;What is this man's crime?&quot;<br /> <b>Jerome:</b> &quot;The Prince has ordered his destruction.&quot;<br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;So be it.&quot;<br /> <br /> The poor sap is held down on the tarp and shown to eternity. The tarp is rolled up and he is carried away.<br /> <br /> Now, you might think little of this scene, but it is very telling. This is the sort of work that clan mekhet usually does. &quot;Your will. Our hands.&quot; That is the credo of Clan Mekhet in Baltimore. If the Prince has ordered the destruction of a vampire, it is the hands of Clan Mekhet that would carry out the duty.<br /> <br /> Alice looks at me and says: &quot;I have been lax in my duties.&quot; She disappears from my sight. I don't see her aside from at dawn and dusk at our haven for several days.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Purge</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice spent the next several days stalking the residents of the Quarantine Zone. Patiently, silently, invisibly she followed them. She made notes on what they said and what they did. She noted who their friends, associates, and coterie mates were. She found out where they slept the daylight hours away. Most importantly, Alice invaded the minds of those kindred we currently held in quarantine. While in their minds she sought only one piece of information: are they, or are they not plotting to overthrow the Prince?<br /> <br /> Once Alice is satisfied that her investigation is complete she takes the information to her Grandsire, Peter (seneschal, childe of the Prince.) Later that week, Alice and I were visiting Antony's bar to talk to him about his duties as Reeve and his lack of action. In fact, we have tried to have this conversation a few times now. Each time, we are interrupted by pressing business. Tonight is not an exception.<br /> <br /> As we are about to begin our conversation, several kindred walk into the bar:<br /> <br /> <b>Kyle:</b> mekhet,<br /> <b>Simon:</b> mekhet, archon, lance, Sire of Kyle<br /> <b>Diana:</b> mekhet, crone<br /> <b>Helen:</b> mekhet, archon, crone, Sire of Diana<br /> <b>Peter:</b> mekhet, seneschal, herald<br /> <br /> The mekhet are accompanied by about a half dozen ghouls. If I haven't made it known before, in addition to being seneschal Peter serves as herald.<br /> <br /> <b>Peter:</b> &quot;By order of the Prince: for three nights hence, no kindred are allowed into the Quarantine Zone with the exceptions of Clans Mekhet and Nosferatu.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, wtf? Such announcements are not unusual in Vampire North Korea (Baltimore.) What is unusual is that the announcement included exceptions for clan Nosferatu in addition to the Mekhet. Has Seville convinced the Prince that the Nosferatu can serve him in the same way the Mkehet do? Have I not served the Prince well? I wanna purge too!<br /> <br /> I step forward and ask Peter what is going on? As I approach, Kyle turns to face me and draws his blade partially from its sheath. I back off. Later at Elysium, I ask Peter for a word. I tell him that I wish to serve the Prince and ask for an exception to the Prince's decree. About an hour later, we are approached by Simon who looks a little annoyed to be serving as messenger to a neonate. He gives us a one word reply from Peter, &quot;Yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> We spend the next three days purging the Quarantine Zone of those kindred who hold in their hearts a desire to overthrow the prince. Don't let me give you the impression that there is a massive conspiracy festering within the Quarantine Zone. Nor are there several independent conspiracies. What we have done here, is separate the intruders from the joiners; the ones who truly want to become citizens of Baltimore from the ones who wish to colonize it for the Council.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean there still aren't trouble makers of various types in residence of the Quarantine Zone. It just means that those that harbor in their hearts a desire to bring harm upon the Prince are gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>We Come Bearing Gifts</u></b><br /> <br /> The Quarantine Zone is getting a little safer these days. Alice and I decide to visit the Zone at about the time when Cooper distributes the blood ration. Also, we bring gifts for a couple of the kindred:<br /> <br /> 1. To Abigail, we gift a rider's crop. She will surely need it to bring Jonathan Poole to heel.<br /> 2. To Jonathon, we gift a small silver whistle. The kind gym teachers carry.<br /> <br /> <b>Alice:</b> &quot;Jonathan, life should be fair. Blow this when you need to declare a time out or foul.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Paralyzed With Indecision</u></b><br /> <br /> So, as I have mentioned there is a sentiment in the city that Antony is not doing a very good job as Reeve. Alice and I decided to visit him and find out what the deal was. our conversation revealed that Antony was dealing with a few issues:<br /> <br /> 1. The position of Reeve is newly created. There is no precedent for Antony to follow. He is worried that if he takes the wrong action he could find himself in hot water.<br /> 2. He has asked some of his former hounds to sign on as deputies to the reeve. As it turns out, neither Spider nor Kade want to sign on to a job with ill defined responsibilities and authority.<br /> 3. Antony has received a letter from Michael Seville asking him to act as Bailiff in Carthian Territories. Antony doesn't know what to do.<br /> <br /> We inform Antony of the mood at Elysium. We tell him that inaction could be just as bad if not worse than the wrong actions in his current position. Further, he should consider the lack of precident an opportunity rather than a liability. We further explain that the letter from Seville is a big opportunity. Seville was one of the Elders opposed to balkanizing the city. By accepting the role of Bailiff in Seville's lands Antony could show the city that central authority is preferable. Further, we reasoned that whatever authority was stripped from the office of the Reeve had been invested in that of Bailiff. By accepting Seville's offer Antony's authority would be made whole (at least in the lands of the Carthians.)<br /> <br /> So, we travelled to visit Seville with Antony in tow. There, we told Seville that Antony would accept his offer but he would need a team of deputies. Seville was only too happy to provide them, but we insisted Antony be able to choose his own team. Seville accepted the terms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Intimidation</u></b><br /> <br /> So, the three of us returned to Antony's bar to discuss candidates to serve as deputies. When we arrive we find an uninvited vampire is waiting for us in the bar. That kindred is Pilgrim (gangrel priscus, archbishop of the lancea sanctum.) Pilgrim is seated on a wooden chair in the center of the room pulled from one of the tables. He is flanked by kneeling page boys (ghouls probably.)<br /> <br /> <b>Pilgrim: </b>&quot;A kindred named Shaman recently entered the city and is trying to gain citizenship. That man has an unfortunate habit and you will make sure that habit ceases.&quot;<br /> <br /> One of the page boys unrolls a scroll featuring a colored pencil portrait of a man (shaman presumably.)<br /> <br /> <b>Pilgrim:</b> &quot;I would ask to secure the assistance of Felix Fox in this affair. He is a man of faith and fortitude.&quot;<br /> <br /> At this point I was getting the impression that Pilgrim was planning to make me do boons for him until he felt I had adequately paid for the daeva twins Alice and I had recently captured. While I was making social calculations in my head, Pilgrim finally got to the point.<br /> <br /> <b>Pilgrim:</b> &quot;Shaman likes to assault clergymen. He has previously practiced his unfortunate habit in the territory of the council, and only against protestants. However, his new residence in the Quarantine Zone brings him in close contact with a Catholic church. The priest of this church is a member of the Jesuit Order. It would be inadvisable for our kind to come into contact with this individual. You may even find your ability to bend the mind of this individual to be ineffective.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Pilgrim:</b> &quot;I do not want you to teach him with words. Use actions. Wait until he is ready to sin and then show him the error of his ways. Rake him over the coals.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pilgrim and I agree that messing around with any organized mortal institution is a bad idea. Especially one with the resources and inclination to believe in the supernatural of the Catholic Church.<br /> <br /> Pilgrim tells Antony that he can either leave the room or pretend he isn't there for the next part. Antony chooses to stay. Pilgrim then turns to one of his page boys and tells them he needs privacy. The pages roll up the scroll, close their eyes tightly and cover their ears. The move a few steps away and hum softly to themselves.<br /> <br /> Pilgrim then turns to me and asks if I have already &quot;changed their memories and made them drink my blood.&quot; He is obviously referring to Aika and Aiko (Alice's and my new toys... I mean loyal retainers.) Although the truth is more complex than that (I didn't change their memories, I used the Stepford Devotion to change their perspective of the events), I simply respond in the affirmative. Also, I am not in the habit of mouthing off to elders.<br /> <br /> Pilgrim then asks if I plan to force to twins to worship the crone or prevent them from attending mass. I respond that I have no such plans.<br /> <br /> <b>Pilgrim: </b>&quot;See that you don't. Otherwise, I may be forced to follow your example and take two for myself.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pilgrim gathers his page boys and leaves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Hindsight</u></b><br /> <br /> The meeting with Pilgrim shook me up a bit. Elders are scary. If I have given you the impression that Felix Fox is this unshakable, unflappable Bruce Willis in Die Hard character, I apologize. The truth is I like to think of him like a slightly emo version of James Kirk. Felix's primary virtue as I see it is that he is not afraid to act. His weakness is that he is ruled by his emotions. Fortunately, I have Alice whose cold vulcan (mekhet) logic is a welcome check to the power of my passions. But I digress.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Alice and I spoke about Pilgrim's display at Antony's bar. We came to the conclusion that he must have acted out of insecurity. I think he sees that Alice and I are the ones with the greatest potential to fuck up his alliance with my Uncle Septimus. He is correct of course (PCs are agents of change after all.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 03-15-2015, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T05:42:44-07:00","id":442433,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Deja Vu</u></b><br /> <br /> Once again, we find ourselves in Antony's bar attempting to complete a conversation that has played out over several nights. We tell Antony that we will help him by serving as deputies, but that we view it as a temporary thing. We will come in, help him right the ship and give him time to train a more permanent staff. And speaking of staff, we propose the following kindred:<br /> <br /> 1. Scarlett (gangrel, neonate, dragon)<br /> 2. Robin (gangrel, neonate, dragon, Scarlett's sister)<br /> 3. Auntie (daeva, neonate)<br /> <br /> None of these kindred would be able to serve as city officials without being made citizens. Scarlett and Robin were easy. They had both been in the kiddie pool since before Alice and me. They had both been slaves of the Order since before Alice and me. They both had been taught the first tier of the Coil of Blood. So, the Order finally saw fit to test their coils and elevate them from their status as Slaves to that of Supplicants. Antony put their names forth to Seville as deputies who in turn put their names forth for citizenship.<br /> <br /> As for Auntie, we asked around and discovered that she had been made an offer to swear fealty and be sponsored into Invictus by Lance Kasson (daeva ancilla invictus.) She wasn't sure what to do. We told her basically that there are a lot more kindred looking to join the First Estate than there were kindred of quality offering bids. Auntie accepted both Lance Kasson's offer and Antony's. She was made citizen soon thereafter in the same way that the gangrel sisters were.<br /> <br /> The three neonates are intended to work as a team. Auntie is the brains of the operation. Scarlett and Robin are the muscle. For the time being, the trio will work only within the inner harbor (kiddy pool) where Antony is much more sure of his authority and therefore less worried about them making mistakes during their training.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Alice and I will serve in the more physically and politically dangerous quarantine zone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Origin Story: Auntie</u></b><br /> <br /> Believe it or not, Alice has been known from time to time to ignore the privacy and boundaries of other kindred. She will slide a little piece of herself into their minds and have a look around. Those most at risk for this treatment are non-citizens. A while ago, Auntie was dropped into the kiddie pool. Back when Alice and I were still living there, she gave Auntie's brain a once over. And as it turns out, Auntie embraced herself.<br /> <br /> A long time ago, during her breathing days, Auntie was a partisan resistance fighter against the Axis forces during the Great Patriotic War. She immigrated to New York City and lived there into old age. One fateful day, she discovered a vampire living in her building's basement. By day, she captured the creature and bound it securely. Over the course of the next several days, she forced it to tell her about vampires, vampire society, and vampire powers by punishing it with starvation and rewarding it with rats.<br /> <br /> In the end, Auntie convinced the vampire that if it would embrace her, she would not kill it. The vampire agreed (under duress.) True to her word, Auntie did not kill her sire. Instead, she travelled to Elysium, presented herself to the authorities, and told them where to find her sire who had just broken the traditions (still prisoner in her old building.)<br /> <br /> Auntie is Daeva, and has shown some talent with Majesty. Her appearance is that of a plump, elderly woman. She usually dresses in second hand clothes. You would be forgiven for assuming she was homeless and ignoring her.<br /> <br /> At one point, Peter (mekhet, seneschal) asked Alice and me for our opinions of the various new residents of the kiddie pool. With regard to Auntie, we told him that we thought she was potentially dangerous. He should recruit her or kill her. Since then, she has proven herself to have a level head, a willingness to deal fairly, and a commitment to the masquerade. I think she's alright.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Law Enforcement in the Quarantine Zone</u></b><br /> <br /> So, Alice and I have been once again saddled with responsibility for law enforcement. Further, the rules might be different from what they were when last we served. Fortunately for us, Michael Seville is easy to talk to. We asked him two questions.<br /> <br /> 1. What are the rules for playing in the Quarantine Zone?<br /> <br /> Answer: He tells us that if we or any other citizens of the city want to play in the quarantine zone and interact with the residents there, we should &quot;play on their level.&quot; Don't go there with overwhelming force and beat the crap out of everyone. Don't go there and try to trick the residents into breaking the laws so they can be punished, etc.<br /> <br /> 2. What are the rules for law enforcement in the Quarantine Zone?<br /> <br /> Answer: Seville tells us that when we are acting as law enforcement on his territory (in his name) we will be expected to be lawful. Further, we should display some sort of symbol of office. When the symbol is visible, we are to act professionally. When the symbol is not on display, we are private citizens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Marco Polo</u></b><br /> <br /> You might recall last chapter I mentioned that we had heard of someone hassling recruits of the Ordo Dracul. Well, I would have liked to look into it sooner but we've been kinda busy. There was only one Slave of the Order in the Quarantine Zone, and that was Patrick Brown (nosferatu, childe of Steward Smiles.) According to Steward (who had been following his childe around under cover of obfuscate like an undead helicopter parent), the ones bothering Patrick were a pair called Marco and Polo. We track the pair down one night and get a look at them. Interestingly, these are the same two vampires who got their asses kicked by werewolves on our territory a little while ago.<br /> <br /> When we caught up with them, they were following a resident of the Quarantine Zone whom I do not recognize. Marco and Polo catch up with the guy and make some threats that if the guy does not give them his tickets, there is going to be violence. The guy is not convinced, and there is violence. Marco and Polo take three red tickets from the beaten down vampire and walk away.<br /> <br /> A few blocks down the road, we confront Marco and Polo. Not about the tickets though. I don't even show my badge. I'm acting as a private citizen here. First, I establish my credibility by reminding them of that time when they got their asses kicked by werewolves. &quot;You stepped onto my territory and got your asses handed to you by a pack of werewolves. Think about it.&quot; Next I inform them that their harassment of future Dragons will cease. They tell me that they were hired to do it. They're just mercenaries. And I soon find out that they are cheap mercs at that.<br /> <br /> Well, they were paid to hassle recruits, not to keep their mouths shut. I bribe them with two Ben Franklins and they tell me that they were hired by a vampire called &quot;Getter.&quot; I thank them for the information, but tell them they are still responsible for their actions against our recruits. Alice and I engage them in fisticuffs, and then bug out. To add insult to injury, we borrow a jar of urine from a bum and pour it over their heads. They are not happy. But hey, they should have thought of that before they went hassling our recruits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Pointing Fingers</u></b><br /> <br /> On our way back to Locust Point, we stop under the bridge. The butcher shop, self storage place, and the mechanics garage where some kindred hang out are all fairly close together here. Tonight we find Sophie (nosferatu, neonate) and strike up a conversation with her. Sophie tells us that she is hungry. Apparently, Marco and Polo have stolen her tickets the last couple times she got them. She could (and does) drink at the butcher shop, but keep in mind that as the almoner Cooper is required by the city to provide only enough blood to keep the beast at bay. Anything more is a boon owed to Cooper. Some know this, some don't.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we ask around and it turns out that Marco and Polo have been stealing a lot of tickets lately. The thing about that is while the tickets are required to feed from mortals in the Quarantine Zone, they are not bearer bonds. They are boons. Boons can be traded, but they cannot be stolen. So, Marco and Polo may be in a bit of trouble here. We once again approach Marco and Polo, who are not too happy with us, what with having to change out of urine soaked clothing and all. However, this time we do flash our badges. We question them to find out if they were acting on their own, or if they were hired (they are mercs after all.) We bribed them with a little cash. We gave them each $100 for each employer whose name they give up. They tell us that they have stolen tickets on behalf of two kindred: Shaman (the priest beater) and EZE.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Judge Felix</u></b><br /> <br /> We gather up Marco, Polo, Shaman, and their accusers (of which there are several.) As a Marshall to the Bailiff of Seville it is within my authority to settle minor disputes like this. We gather in the nearby abandoned mechanics garage which has a few couches, tables, and chairs.<br /> <br /> I dispense with the Latin and ask if anyone minds if I conduct this business in the vernacular. There are no objections. So, we spend some time questioning witnesses. To make a long story short, the two doods (not Sophie in this case) who had their tickets stolen by Marco and Polo on behalf of Shaman had recently borrowed some tickets from Shaman. When Shaman came to ask for them back, they refused. After all, they were hungry too. So, Marco and Polo were hired to recover the debt. Of the three tickets owed, Marco and Polo kept 1 and gave 2 back to Shaman.<br /> <br /> I therefore ruled that the debtor now owed 3 tickets each to Marco and Polo to be paid within 2 months time. Remember, boons are legally enforceable currency. Refusing to repay a boon will mean that you will owe a boon to any kindred who &quot;help&quot; you honor your bargain.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of confused faces and a collective &quot;WTF!?!&quot; from the spectators to the proceeding, but I do not explain my decision.<br /> <br /> After the trial, I ask Marco and Polo (who are much better inclined to cooperate with me now) where they think I could find EZE. They tell me that they can tell me where his hangouts are for free, or for a small bribe they can tell me where he will be tonight. I give the bribe. Marco and Polo tell us that EZE is planning to attack the haven of Eve Liebsch later tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Penthouse</u></b><br /> <br /> Eve had been living in the Kiddy Pool since the very beginning of the game. For whatever reason, she was demoted to the Quarantine Zone when it opened up. She was living in a top floor apartment of the only decent building in the area. This apartment was previously inhabited by Merry (the daeva girl who blood bound Matilde, a dragon and childe of Bartholomew.) Anyway, Alice and I were aware that this haven of Eve's is a proper haven. She has permission and recognition of Michael Seville, granting full legal protections to this haven.<br /> <br /> So, Alice and I arrive at the door of Eve's apartment and knock. Eve opens the door and we tell her that later this night, EZE is going to come attack her in her haven. Eve thanks us for the info and starts making plans to leave. We ask instead for permission to enter her haven and defend it from attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Alice:</b> &quot;May we have permission to come inside and help you defend what's yours? We would agree to do this in exchange for... a bag of popcorn.&quot;<br /> <br /> Eve's ghoul does in fact have popcorn in the kitchen. We accept our payment and enter Eve's Domain. When EZE arrives with three ghouls and breaks down the door, Eve and her ghoul run for the bedroom. A moment later, Alice and I drop our cloak of obfuscate and attack them from behind. We have them surrounded. Well, the guy didn't come prepared for even numbers. We prevail. Once EZE is subdued, we interrogate him using Dominate. Here is what we learned:<br /> <br /> 1. He has been forcing kindred to drink his blood. There are a few others whom he has forced into a blood bond.<br /> 2. He planned to do the same with Eve.<br /> 3. He himself works for a nosferatu from Council territory named Elliot. (I'm sensing a pattern)<br /> <br /> We've heard enough. We make a call to Spider (nosferatu, all around cool guy) who works for Seville. We want him to come help us with the transport of these prisoners. When he arrives, he is leading a mortal woman by the neck. To a casual observer, they might be lovers. they are both smiling and walking arm in arm. Anything more than casual observation will reveal that he is escorting her by force and threatening her with violence (and nightmare) if she doesn't put on a good smile.<br /> <br /> Spider informs us that he found her hiding in the bushes outside and thought she might have something to do with whatever was going on here. So next, we question the girl. She is here because her regnant has gone missing. Her vampire had some kind of disagreement with EZE and now she can't find him. EZE (still compelled to tell the truth by Dominate) tells us that her Regnant refused to drink his blood. There was violence and he wound up in torpor. He hid the body in his storage unit by digging up some concrete and pouring a new batch over him.<br /> <br /> EZE, his ghouls, the torpid vampire's ghoul, Spider, Alice, and I all travel north to the old armory building which was used by the late sheriff Elliot Rex. The archon Helen is called, and she brings final death to EZE and his ghouls. The torpid vampire's ghoul is brought to the quarantine zone where I have promised her she can recover her regnant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>At the Self Storage</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I arrive at the self storage with the girl ghoul. We break into the unit formerly occupied by EZE. At this point a small crowd gathers wanting to know why we were breaking into someone's unit. Before we can enter, three vampires show up. These are the ones whose blood bond we have just broken. Instead of being grateful, they have arrived wanting to do Alice and Me harm.<br /> <br /> One of them is armed with a weird evil looking blade, about the size of a knife colored a dark crimson and seemingly made of roiling blood. Well let me tell you, it's a good thing I have purchased close quarters combat style. I was easily able to disarm the dood and with one tiny poke he fell instantly into torpor; a fate that was apparently meant to be mine.<br /> <br /> With the help of a few bystanders, the remaining vampire attackers are restrained and torpored. We once again call Michael Seville and meet him at the old armory, and once again the Archon Helen is called to bring an end to these vampires.<br /> <br /> As for the super scary knife, it now looked like a shiv made of broken glass with a duct tape handle. I carefully wrapped it in garbage bags and more duct tape until what we had was a big duct tape puck. I asked Septimus to get me a meeting with Pilgrim. When he asks me why and I tell him, he says &quot;Maybe it's better if I just take this to him for you.&quot; Anyway, I had a hunch this blade was created using evil Belial's Brood magic, and I thought Pilgrim should know.<br /> <br /> Finally, the ghoul girl is allowed to unearth her regnant, who is fed with blood from Cooper's butcher shop through a funnel before being awakened. Happy endings are beautiful.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Getter</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I are starting to get tired. We are being run ragged this way and that. Between cleaning up after Dorris Bettes and dodging bullets sent by Elliot Jr. All I want to do is drink tasty blood and pursue leisure activities. Is that too much to ask? Apparently, it is.<br /> <br /> So, Marco and Polo are both prolific and affordable in their mercenary work. As you know, it was them who were hassling Patrick Brown about the Dragons. At first glance, it would appear that they were hassling him to get him to join the Carthians, but they were also trying to get the location of the chapter house out of him. Once again a small bribe is paid to the duo to get the identity of their boss. &quot;Hey, they should have thought to pay us not to tell. They didn't.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, there is a vampire named &quot;Getter.&quot; He is also a Quarantine Zone resident. We speak to him and rough him up a little to discover that he was sent here from Council Territory by Sunny (daeva, dragon)<br /> <br /> A while ago we met two kindred in council territory who claimed to be dragons. I haven't mentioned it before because it hasn't become relevant to the story until now. Anyway, the dragons both claimed to be supplicants. Sunny was here from New York. He left the city to avoid his mortal family. Ralph (the other dragon) was here from Shreveport Louisiana. He and his sire came all this way to recover a book stolen from their chapter house by the same team who were ransacking Bartholomew's haven a while back. The same book that Susan received as a prize from Pilgrim for being one of the winners of the Golden Ticket Hunt way back when.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we inform Konrad that some shady characters are trying to discover the location of the chapter house via violence and intimidation. Konrad orders us to &quot;take the Axe and get to the bottom of the situation. Inform the others that the chapter house is closed until further notice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Sunny</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice, Kade (gangrel, dragon), Enrique (ventrue, dragon, axe sworn), and I travel to Council Territory in search of Sunny. When we find him and he lays eyes on Alice and me, he gets a weird look on his face and attacks. He keeps telling us that he wants to kill us, but he does it with a weird tone of voice. Kade and Enrique restrain him and we spend some time undoing the Dominate job which has been done on him. Once he is freed he begins to celebrate.<br /> <br /> <b>Sunny:</b> &quot;I Knew it. I knew if I sent Getter he would be sloppy and you would find me. Who's awesome? I'm awesome!&quot;<br /> <br /> At this time, we discover that assigning Patrick to Felicity's diner's club delayed Getter from finding the location of the chapter house. After all, it's hard to extort info from a group of six kindred who are traveling together prepared for battle. However, Getter used a different tactic, and although it took him a long time to lurk and follow random kindred he did eventually find the location and report it to Sunny.<br /> <br /> Sunny, in turn reported that information to Pat, the ventrue who compelled his obedience with Dominate. Are we in time to do anything? Sunny tells us that Pat left about 15 minutes ago in a bright green pickup truck. So, we sprang into action:<br /> <br /> 1. We hauled ass back to the university where the chapter house is located.<br /> 2. We got Scarlett and Robin (gangrel sisters, new deputies) and asked them to take to the air in search of a bright green pickup truck.<br /> 3. The two find our quarry and the now 6 of us travel to intercept them. I have recently acquired Obfuscate 5 (1.0 cloak the gathering, not the newfangled holodeck version)<br /> <br /> In the backyard of a residential neighborhood not too far from the university, there is a bright green pickup truck and two black vans. Gathered around them are three vampires and twice as many ghouls standing around a marked up map.<br /> <br /> <b>Pat: </b>&quot;There will be a convoy of 4 cars travelling along this route. The girl will be in the second one. The plan is to ram the car, take the girl, and rabbit out of there.&quot;<br /> <br /> Christina is grounded at the moment, but Susan is not. These days, she travels pretty exclusively between my Grandsire's estate and Elysium. When She travels, she usually only takes two cars, but since the last family meeting she has beefed things up. Anyway, we've heard enough.<br /> <br /> We attack. There is violence, but it is over quickly. We arrived with a lot of muscle and attacked from stealth. So, we question Pat with a combination of Dominate and Auspex. Here is what we learned:<br /> <br /> 1. Pat was working for a nosferatu named Elliot. (big surprise)<br /> 2. He was recruited in New Jersey and paid one gold bar up front. He was promised a second gold bar upon completion of the contract.<br /> 3. The plan is for him to kidnap Susan or Christina and bury them in the basement of a house with dirt floors in the barrens between Baltimore and Council Territory.<br /> 4. Once he has done so, he is to paint a graffiti peace sign in a certain alley.<br /> 5. The gold will be waiting for him in Jersey when he returns.<br /> <br /> The vampires and ghouls are all killed. We ask Calypso for access to the grave yard to dispose of some corpses. As long as we promise not to disturb the older graves we are good to go. So, Alice, the gangrel sisters, and I spend the night digging up pauper's graves and installing roommates. All such graves are sprinkled liberally with salt. (I know we are not playing Sam and Dean style Supernatural, but there is nothing wrong with a little caution.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Common Interests</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I meet with Belinski (nosferatu, invictus, brother of the late Sheriff Elliot Rex) and Jerome James (nosferatu, carthian childe of Elliot Rex, brother of Elliot Jr.) We explain to them that their nephew/brother is in town and ask them if there is any love lost between them.<br /> <br /> Belinski reaches into his pocket and produces a letter with a red ribbon. It is an indulgence for destruction of a vampire given by the prince.<br /> <br /> <b>Belinski:</b> &quot;I have carried this with me every night since the death of my brother.&quot;<br /> <br /> Belinski and Jerome are in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Dead Drop</u></b><br /> <br /> So, we talk to Susan and convince her not to leave our Grandsire's estate until further notice. She is not happy, but she will do it. Next, we get a mannequin and dress it in some of Susan's clothes. The mannequin is put in to a large duffle. Using Obfuscate 4 to appear vaguely like Pat I travel to the house where the drop is supposed to take place. I carry the mannequin to the basement and bury it under the dirt floor. From there, I travel to the specified alley. I use dominate to make a passerby spray paint the requisite peace sign and then forget about doing it.<br /> <br /> Belinski has agreed to keep the house under surveillance and contact us when it is go time.<br /> <br /> Now, we wait.<br /> <br /> <br /> We play tonight. I'm all giddy with excitement!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T08:31:05-07:00","id":444306,"title":"","content":"New Felix entries fresh from the weekend? Nice way to start the week:3<br /> <br /> However, i had a minor wtf moment while reading. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/437815-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-7?p=442390#post442390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Tag</u></b><br /> <br /> One night Kyle (mekhet, neonate, childe of the archon Simon) approaches Alice and me. He tells us that one of the new Quarantine Zone residents has made a mistake. During a conversation with Terry (mekhet, carthian, newest citizen) he asked her, &quot;Who is the stupid bitch that made you a citizen?&quot; Well, the Prince made Terry a citizen. The Prince does not tolerate insults, regardless of how minor.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> Pip is sent to final death via a series of dozens of tiny puncture wounds. Sucks to be him. On the bright side, it isn't Alice and me who are tasked with dealing with the body. Woot!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only the punishment seems overtly disproportionate (i get we are in a dictatorial regimen, yes) but taking into account that the vampire didn't even knew who was the subject he was talking about i'd expect a simple (yet effective) beatdown would suffice. Moreso, i had a distinct &quot;giggle moment&quot; feeling about the way of execution and overall behaviour during the scene that left me asking myself about Felix's Humanity score.<br /> <br /> PS. The Nosferatu Clan seems to be growing in power and influence, and i cannot deny i enjoy the perspective of Seville as Prince. How does Alice, however, feels about that uprising? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:03:22-07:00","id":445888,"title":"","content":"Felix's humanity score is 5. Although I don't think killing vampires is a breaking point in the humanity system. After all, what act is more human than murder? Even so, this was not a murder, it was an execution. I don't know who ordered the execution of Pip, but I would bet money that it was Peter.<br /> <br /> When the immigrants started flooding the city from Council Territory, Peter was not happy. Neither were Felix and Alice. Peter has made clear his feelings that we should as much as possible find reasons to destroy the interlopers. Every immigrant who gains citizenship in Baltimore is one less kindred who a native could have embraced instead. There are after all a limited number of kindred a given city can support.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the Nosferatu: You are correct that Clan Nosferatu has been gaining influence in the city, but it would be more accurate to say that Michael Seville has been gaining influence in the city. During last night's session we found out that Seville has successfully recruited a few more kindred to his banner.<br /> <br /> Some people have mentioned that they think Michael Seville acts a lot like an Invictus vampire. And they are not wholly wrong, but Seville also differs from Invictus in key ways.<br /> <br /> 1. He actually listens to the ideas of other kindred, even young ones, and sometimes puts them into practice.<br /> 2. He does not give preferential treatment to vampires based on their covenant affiliations. Being Carthian isn't enough to earn favor from Seville, nor is being Invictus enough to earn disdain. Michael Seville judges individuals by their actions.<br /> 3. He tolerates opposing viewpoints. For example, the late sheriff was his only true opposition within the carthian movement in Baltimore. Elliot Rex and Michael Seville disagreed with each other about a lot of things, but Seville did not use his influence to squash the ancilla sheriff.<br /> 4. Michael Seville believes that vampires should be free to choose their own covenants.<br /> <br /> <br /> After last night's game I asked the ST about my grandsire. I know so much about Michael Seville and how he does things, and even though I have seen so little of the Prince I feel I know him well because I live in the city He has created for us. Konrad Von Berg on the other hand is something of a mystery. He so rarely gives his opinions. So, my ST shared some meta-game knowledge with us.<br /> <br /> 1. Konrad Von Berg is the least personally powerful elder in the city. His strength comes from the fact that he has his family and they are all loyal to him.<br /> 2. Konrad Von Berg has long ago thought about what it means to be Ventrue Priscus and ally of the Prince. And based on those thoughts he made the decision to forge his clan (famiy) and his covenant (ordo dracul) into weapons which could be wielded in defense of the city.<br /> <br /> The Prince has done something similar with his clan.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the rambling. To answer your second question: Alice is not too happy about the situation. Not because she doesn't like Seville or the nosferatu of the city, but because seeing the nosferatu perform duties which are the responsibility of the mekhet leads her to believe that she has personally failed the city and failed the Prince. She has responded by redoubling her efforts to take on the responsibilities which mekhet are expected to take on.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:55:50-07:00","id":447698,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the explanation and the write ups, they are awesome.<br /> <br /> My question about Alice's feelings was founded not only in her reaction (her self-dissappointment was clear - by the way, here's another theory: given that the Mekhetocracy is essentially the Prince's Cult... could be bloodbound Alice, and in fact, all of them, to the Prince? Their loyalty and love seem unusually strong-) but also in the fact that those were <b>Nosferatu</b> were doing <b>Mekhet</b> job.<br /> <br /> My first reaction was: <i>&quot;these guys are clearly lying to Felix. The Prince would never rely on Nosferatu when he has their Mekhet to do exactly this kind of things&quot;</i>. I was somewhat surprised Felix believed their words without further questions. <br /> <br /> My second reaction was: <i>&quot;what the hell is going on in Baltimore with the Nosfies? They are clearly rising in the power structure if they have for real this new position&quot;</i>. And given the dictatorial way of power in Baltimore, i would see that as a Prince weakness... not that i'd share those thoughts with anyone else xD<br /> <br /> That's why i was asking about Alice. I thought that maybe she would have felt similar feelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T09:52:40-07:00","id":447866,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Prince intends to pass praxis to Seville and this is a way of getting Seville to establish his own thought police.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T17:53:12-07:00","id":448540,"title":"","content":"@Phersus: I really don't think the Prince has blood bound Alice and the other Mekhet. He doesn't need to. The only mekhet who survive the Kiddie Pool are precisely those that can be convinced to drink the Kool-Aid. There were other siblings in Alice's brood. None of them survived.<br /> <br /> Further, I can see how you might think I was being lied to when Spider, Jerome, and Sam arrived with a tarp and killed that vampire. However, I happen to know that that these three nossies work directly for Michael Seville. Further, I presume that any citizens of the city have long since learned not to take the name of the Prince in vain.<br /> <br /> I have mentioned above that clans ventrue and mekhet have been forged into weapons by their prisci. Michael Seville ran his clan differently. He once told me that the pressure of the nosferatu clan curse will over time either crush a vampire or make of him a diamond. His policy with regard to his clan was to patiently wait for diamonds to form naturally. Well, my guess is that Seville changed his mind on the efficacy of his wait and see policy and has chosen to take a more active role in the formation of diamonds within his clan.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I think the truth is closer to Audrey's theory. Although I don't think the Prince has yet made his decision, I do think this was an opportunity for Seville to do a test run with his clan. Whether this is an audition of sorts or just a shake-down cruise... I don't know. I suspect it's both.<br /> <br /> One more thing regarding the execution of Pip: The action was not taken simply to punish a minor thought crime. There were two other reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. To harden Betty. Betty is the youngest member of the mekhetocracy. She needs to get used to being a stone cold killer when she is called. If we were using the new humanity rules, all mekhet would sooner or later get a bane and the associated soul scars to prevent breaking points when carrying out violence on behalf of the Prince/Mekhetocracy.<br /> <br /> 2. Practice. You may remember a few chapters back that the Prince personally led an attack against a visiting Elder of the Lancea Sanctum. During the attack, the tactic was for each of us to attack from stealth, roll away, and reestablish obfuscate. Pip provided a much less dangerous opponent for the newer members of the mekhetocracy to practice this tactic on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T18:52:16-07:00","id":470574,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Elliot Jr.</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I have been distracted for the past few days while we wait to hear from Belinsky (nosferatu, ancilla, invictus, brother of Elliot Rex) about the results of the dead drop. In less than a week we got word that someone had been inside the house where we buried the Susan Small decoy. We set out prepared for battle and brought backup with us in the form of Jerome James (nosferatu, neonate, childe of Elliot Rex) and a few of his ghouls.<br /> <br /> We travel to Council Territory and catch the trail of Elliot Jr. Alice, Sidney (my ghoul), and I were the forward observers. When we spotted Elliot leaving the Council Elysium, we didn't have time to regroup with Jerome and his ghouls. Alice, Sidney (my ghoul), and I travelled together using Obfsuscate 5 (1e version.) We followed Elliot Jr. and two other vampires north out of Council Territory and into the barrens.<br /> <br /> We wait for an opportune moment to strike, and I hit Elliot over the head with a sap. Rather than responding with violence, Elliot turns around and begins talking.<br /> <br /> <b>Elliot:</b> &quot;What the fuck Felix? Are you crazy?&quot; He begins talking nonsense and trying to look like the aggrieved party to his vampire pals. Well, I was initially confused by this, but soon enough decided that I wasn't going to deal with this bullshit. There is violence, and Elliot runs while Alice and I are occupied with his vampire pals. Sidney gives chase to Elliot and is able to slow Elliot enough that Alice and I are able to catch him. The end result of the combat is a torpored Elliot Jr. and two beaten down vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Beaten down Vampire:</b> &quot;You think the Council will let you get away with this?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;This is not Council Territory. Run back to mommy if you want, but if you come out here you're on your own.&quot; (we were currently in the barrens approximately equidistant to Council Territory, Roy's territory, and Baltimore proper.<br /> <br /> So, we pack up and bring Elliot back to our haven where every precaution is taken to ensure he does not escape. We are not going to rely solely on his current torpor for security. We then contacted both Belinsky and his nephew Jerome James that we have Elliot Jr. (Bellinsky's other nephew.) Bellinsky arrives and we hand Elliot Jr. over to him.<br /> <br /> <b>Felix:</b> &quot;I trust we will have no more trouble from your nephew.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Warnings and Intercessions</u></b><br /> <br /> A week or two later, we were having a discussion with Michael Seville.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;Why on earth did you not kill Elliot Jr. when he was in your custody? Why would you release him to his Uncle. He is still alive, you know. And he is telling stories to his uncle.&quot;<br /> <br /> Apparently, Bellinsky has awakened Elliot Jr. for questioning. He is still being held prisoner, but the two have been having conversations. Elliot Jr. has been telling his uncle that he couldn't possibly have been the diablerist that killed his sire. He is pointing the finger at me and saying that with my ventrue powers who knows of what I am capable. Further, I would certainly have motive as Elliot Rex killed my Sire.<br /> <br /> I told Seville that Elliot Jr. was Bellinsky's family and it was therefore his responsibility to deal with him, and I had given my word that I would give him over. Plus, he was the one with an indulgence from the Prince to bring final death to Elliot Jr. However, I did assure Seville that I would speak with Bellinsky's Liege Lord.<br /> <br /> I arranged a meeting with my Uncle Septimus and informed him of the situation. He didn't think it would be a good idea to simply order Bellinsky to kill his nephew. That action would probably sew more seeds of doubt that Elliot Jr. ever could.<br /> <br /> Finally, we went to speak to Octavia (our mentor.) Octavia in turn spoke to the Archon Simon (ancilla, lancea sanctum, mekhet.) She called in a boon with the archon. Simon in turn went to speak with Bellinsky.<br /> <br /> On the night Elliot Rex was discovered to have been diablerized, Simon was one of the Mekhet present at the crime scene. Simon told Bellinsky that he was at the scene, and that he ran his fingers through the ashes of Elliot Rex. He can tell Bellinsky that regardless of what Elliot Jr. has told him, it was in fact Elliot Jr. who drank the heart's blood of Elliot Rex.<br /> <br /> Bellinsky listens to this and decides to kill his nephew. This is a relief, I guess, but the seeds of doubt have still been sown in the mind of Bellinsky as regards his loyalty to my family. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have about two sessions worth of stories to write up at this point. I'll try to get it done this week. Thanks for reading this rather short update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T06:56:46-07:00","id":472663,"title":"","content":"Moarrrr :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T10:27:56-07:00","id":504365,"title":"","content":"This is a threat: i have necro-thread-mantic powers and i will use them to make you continue Felix and Alice story, figurehead! <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> (So please, continue it so i can keep bragging about my kewl summoning powerz :P)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T11:04:49-07:00","id":504385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/437815-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-7?p=470574#post470574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have about two sessions worth of stories to write up at this point. I'll try to get it done this week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would anyone write something like that and then <b><u>not</u></b> post the session recap? How could anyone be so cruel? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/640-bram_pc","name":"Bram_pc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T11:55:52-07:00","id":504451,"title":"","content":"As it has been silent for a while here, I also want to add that I love this Actual Play. I am anticipating its continuation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T06:55:08-07:00","id":505392,"title":"","content":"Hey thanks for the kind words everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry I have been so late. I got hit with the overtime hammer at work. I'm pulling 50 hour weeks these days. I'll try to find the time to type again soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T11:06:31-07:00","id":505805,"title":"","content":"Thanks for taking the time full stop :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T12:57:46-07:00","id":505990,"title":"","content":"Thank you, summoning powers! Er... i mean, figurehead. May the strength be with you so you can kick the a** of your super busy schedule mate! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T17:22:22-07:00","id":507401,"title":"","content":"I started the write up a month ago, but didn't get around to finish it. Here is what I have so far. More to come. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Concerning Council Territory</u></b><br /> <br /> Of the four territories that border Baltimore, Council Territory has turned out to be the most... colorful. Apparently, there are several packs of werewolves who make their homes nearby and one or two of them have been having skirmishes with the vampires of the Council. Over the course of the game, we have had some inkling that something like this might be happening.<br /> <br /> Flashback 1: Remember the Golden Ticket Hunt organized by Pilgrim? It took place in the forest south of Council Territory. That night, Elliot Jr. and his coterie captured a werewolf. Alice and I set him free before things escalated into an interspecies casus belli.<br /> <br /> Flashback 2: When Mandy O'Kelly came to Alice and me because she was convinced Appollonia was going to kill her, one of the reasons she gave us to suspect that the Daeva Elder was less than loyal to Mandy and to the city was that she (Appollonia) was having meetings with werewolves near council territory.<br /> <br /> It turns out that prior to his death, Elliot Rex (nosferatu, ancilla, former sheriff) was providing consultation and material support to the Council in their conflict with the werewolves. Since his demise, the council has been slowly losing ground against their furry foes.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons that so many vampires have been arriving in the Quarantine Zone in an attempt to gain Baltimore Citizenship.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Bring Us Your Hungry... Yearning to be Free</u></b><br /> <br /> You will probably be hearing a lot of unfamiliar names in these chapters. In character there are a lot of new faces showing up in the Quarantine Zone. Out of character, even I am having trouble keeping them straight. According to the ST, this is an opportunity to fill out the ranks of the pyramid below Alice and me, so that we are not perpetually the newest citizens of Baltimore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Responsibilities</u></b><br /> <br /> When Alice and I signed up to help cousin Antony with his new responsibilities as Reeve of the City and Bailiff of Michael Seville, we made two things clear:<br /> <br /> 1. We needed cool titles. We did not want to be compared to dogs, favorably or otherwise. This is how we got the title of Marshal.<br /> <br /> 2. This would be a temporary assignment. Alice and I were here to get things in order, bring the level of chaos down to a dull roar, and give Antony a chance to catch his breath and select/train new marshals.<br /> <br /> When we reported to Michael Seville for duty (we would be serving in the Quarantine Zone, Seville's Domain), he basically said that he wasn't sure how soon he would be willing to let us resign. Well, one out of two ain't bad.<br /> <br /> So, Alice and I have been spending a lot of time across the bay, babysitting the newcomers and testing them for rabies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Jiffy-Lube</u></b><br /> <br /> There is an old closed down oil change place not too far from the butcher shop where Cooper (daeva, almoner) distributes the blood ration to the newcomers. Someone has taken it upon themselves to drag in some furniture and use the place as a kindred hangout.<br /> <br /> One night, I am approached by Miles (daeva, carthian.) He wants me to escort him out of the Quarantine Zone so he can visit both Michael Seville, and the City Elysium. He is offering to consider the favor a boon, so I agree to take him. We stop by Seville's office and after a short wait, Miles is allowed into Seville's inner office. I am not privy to his conversation with Seville.<br /> <br /> From there, we travel to the City Elysium. Miles looks around and asks to speak with Madeline Ross (daeva, keeper of Elysium, ancilla.) Christina notices the three of us talking and wanders over. I casually offer my arm so Christina can come close and listen in.<br /> <br /> <b>Miles:</b> (stammering a bit) &quot;Well... we have made this place. A place where kindred can gather and talk without fear of violence, and I was um... kinda hoping you would be willing to make that place and official Elysium.<br /> <br /> The Keeper invites Miles upstairs to talk more about it and I follow them. Christina pulls on my arm and I hang back long enough for her to whisper in my ear, &quot;You can't allow this to happen.&quot; (Christina has had permission to create an official Elysium for a year or two now, but has yet to pull the trigger. She doesn't want more competition.)<br /> <br /> Madame Ross leads us upstairs and says, &quot;Well, let's go see this place. But first, do you have any money on you? or valuables?&quot; Miles indicates that he has a Rolex watch. It looks expensive.<br /> <br /> <b>Madame Ross:</b> &quot;Good. Please place it there.&quot; She points to a plate in plain sight.<br /> <b>Miles:</b> &quot;Please. It has sentimental value...&quot;<br /> <b>Madame Ross:</b> &quot;You wanted to play the game. So play.&quot;<br /> <br /> Reluctantly, Miles leaves his watch on the plate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Elysium?</u></b><br /> <br /> Together, we travel to the Quarantine Zone. Madame Ross wants to see the proposed site of the new Elysium before she grants it her blessing. We arrive at the Jiffy-Lube and Madame Ross spends less than thirty seconds inside before we leave. While standing in the parking lot, she takes off a rather expensive looking bracelet and turns to Miles. The bracelet is gold, and contains many precious gems.<br /> <br /> <b>Madame Ross:</b> &quot;Mr. Miles, would you please take this bracelet and place it on the coffee table inside? Hurry back.&quot;<br /> <br /> Miles disappears into the Jiffy-Lube and returns shortly. We have a pleasant conversation for about five minutes before the Keeper turns to Miles again and says, &quot;Mr. Miles, may I have my bracelet back?&quot;<br /> <br /> Miles gives the keeper a slightly confused look before once again entering the Jiffy-Lube. he returns a few minutes later with a crestfallen look on his face.<br /> <br /> <b>Miles:</b> &quot;I'm sorry Madame Ross, your bracelet is missing...&quot;<br /> <b>Madame Ross:</b> &quot;I see. Marshal, please see to the return of my property.&quot;<br /> <br /> The three of us travel once again to the city Elysium where Mile's watch is still sitting on the plate, in plain sight. Miles puts his watch back on, and I escort him back to the Quarantine Zone and his obviously not-an-Elysium Jiffy-Lube.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Case of the Missing Bracelet</u></b><br /> <br /> Grumble... stoopid newcomers making me do extra work. Well, the Keeper of Elysium is a very influential individual and I do kinda like her, so I get to work. Well, no one in the Jiffy-Lube saw anything (big surprise) so we moved on and started canvassing the local pawn shops. It took some application of Auspex and Dominate, but we did locate and recover the bracelet.<br /> <br /> The Bracelet was sold to a pawn shop for a lot less than its value. According to the pawn broker, he estimated he could fence it for $50,000 and he bought it for only $1,000. With Dominate, we convinced him to sell the bracelet to us for $1,000 and then left him with no memory of the bracelet or how he came into possession of it.<br /> <br /> From there, we started questioning the newcomers who were present at the Jiffy-Lube at the time of the theft. Near the shore of the bay, we came upon a young vamp named Piper Morgan. She was ranting to some other vamps about equality.<br /> <br /> <b>Piper Morgan:</b> &quot;Have you noticed that women get fed on more often than men? And have you noticed that women get made into ghouls more often than men? Get turned into slaves more often than men? It's sexist!&quot;<br /> <br /> We asked Piper for a moment of her time and asked her about the bracelet. She was unaware she had done anything wrong and wasn't shy about admitting that she took it. So, we dragged her into the recently vacated storage locker of the late EZE and chopped off one of her hands with a meat cleaver we had purchased from Cooper's butcher shop.<br /> <br /> You might be thinking WTF Felix? Why are you such a dick? Isn't that a bit harsh? Well, first I do not particularly care for most of the newcomers from Council Territory. Any of them who become citizens will take up positions that could have been filled by the childer of Baltimore Citizens. Second, I did Piper a favor. As a Marshal, my authority and the severity of punishments I can levy are limited. If I had decided to give her a slap on the wrist, there would be the very real possibility that someone could have appealed to a higher authority in favor of a harsher punishment. This potential appeal could have come months or even years in the future. The fact that I used as harsh a punishment as I was authorized to use makes a potential appeal much less likely to be brought up or even to succeed if it is. I have effectively closed the issue for Piper. Her hand will grow back in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T02:55:34-07:00","id":507895,"title":"","content":"Harsh, but fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T04:20:55-07:00","id":507938,"title":"","content":"Nice post. I specially enjoyed that Rolex/bracelet scene: classy and precise. Whoever is your ST, compliment him. As for Felix being a dick... would not think that by this decision. It was deserved, at least from uppers perspective. And after all some harsh attitude is needed when you represent the autority. Pipper Morgan could dissagree, tho <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T05:09:10-07:00","id":508865,"title":"","content":"Was the hand of a vampire so stupid and self-absorbed that she actually drags down the collective average IQ of vampires worth $1000? Because I think Felix and Alice got jipped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T03:18:33-07:00","id":509764,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Ghouls</u></b><br /> <br /> In Baltimore, blood slaves to the immortals are generally not referred to as ghouls. Instead, they have one of two designations depending upon their place (or lack thereof) in vampire society.<br /> <br /> <b>Attendants</b> are those mortals, usually ghouls, who are told the truth (more or less) about their condition and made aware of the all night society. They are members of it, and do have some protections under the law; although they are still considered the property of their regnant.<br /> <br /> <b>Retainers</b> are also often ghouls, but they are kept in the dark about the truth of vampire nature, society, etc, and they are forbidden from being taken to places where kindred gather. They are not considered members of society and have little protection under the law.<br /> <br /> In the event that a ghoul is killed by another vampire and the matter reaches the courts, the level of restitution that may be ordered will be quite different. In the case of retainers, the restitution would be akin to replacing a broken vase. Attendants are another matter.<br /> <br /> To my knowledge, there have been no cases involving the destruction of someone's ghoul since they were designated as ghouls/retainers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Mouse</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice's attendant was born as Cooper's mortal sister before he was embraced. For details of how she came to be Alice's ghoul check out Kiddie Pool Saga Part 1 and do a keyword search for &quot;boy meets girl.&quot; Mouse was seventeen when she was made a ghoul about five years ago. Unlike my ghoul Sidney whose life is completely controlled by vitae and dominate, Mouse is given certain levels of freedom.<br /> <br /> for example, Mouse is allowed to travel freely within Alice's and my territory, as well as the territory of my cousin Antony. She has even made friends with Tigger (Terry's ghoul) and the two of them occasionally socialize. Mouse is also permitted to visit the city Elysium, where there is an area specifically open to Attendants.<br /> <br /> Mouse is insatiably curious and she does not understand the concept &quot;none of my business.&quot; She is small of stature and easy to overlook. We often use her for daytime surveillance missions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>New Neighbors</u></b><br /> <br /> So... one night, the doorbell rings. I don't bother to answer, I have attendants for that. Mouse comes to me and says she hasn't answered the door because she does not recognize the person outside. So, I do it. On the other side of the door is a conservatively dressed woman in her early 40s. <a href=\"http://s9.postimg.org/lyrvdlqyn/neighboor.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">She is holding a tray on which sits a dessert made of jell-o</a>.<br /> <br /> We have a short conversation in which she explains that she and her family (husband and two teenage sons) are new to the neighborhood. Her husband is the manager of the new manufacturing plant that is opening nearby. (believe it or not, all this new development is not wholly vampire driven. There is a new manufacturing plant in the area that has been bringing hundreds of new jobs to the area)<br /> <br /> Anyway, she eventually reminds me that her arms are getting tired from holding the tray and I take it from her with a smile and a &quot;thank you.&quot; She departs and I walk to the kitchen. Further inspection of the dessert reveals it to bear a striking resemblance to a pair of breasts.<br /> <br /> I smirk and then deposit the dessert into the trash. We are far too paranoid in this household to allow our Attendants to eat desserts that may or may not be drugged/poisoned. Nevertheless, Mouse was disappointed.<br /> <br /> <b>Mouse:</b> &quot;Hey! I wanted to eat some of that.&quot; (pouty face.)<br /> <br /> I turn to Mouse and order her to make friends with the new neighbors so we can find out if we can take their presence at face value, or if there is something else going on. We also concoct a cover story in which Mouse is my little sister and I have been taking care of her since our parents died.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Case of the Dead Attendant</u></b><br /> <br /> One night while visiting the Quarantine Zone, we are approached by a small group of kindred. They tell me that they have captured a lawbreaker and that I have to do something about it. Among the group are:<br /> <br /> Miles (daeva, carthian)<br /> Charles Wood (not much info about this guy yet.)<br /> Getter (the dood who discovered the location of the OD Chapter house)<br /> <br /> Getter is the plaintiff. According to him, one of his ghouls was minding his own business when he was shot in the head without provocation by a vampire named Patrick. At this point, I have not had more than an introduction with Charles Wood, and even less with Getter. So, I decide to send for Patrick and settle this dispute.<br /> <br /> Once everyone is assembled, I begin asking questions. There are four things I want to know:<br /> <br /> 1. Most important: was the body disposed of discretely? (masquerade preservation)<br /> 2. Did Patrick kill the ghoul?<br /> 3. Why did he do it?<br /> 4. Was the ghoul in question an Attendant or a Retainer?<br /> <br /> In the course of my questioning, I find out that Miles is here merely to observe because he has an interest in matters political and legal. As I was asking questions, I was very frustrated. No one was interested in giving me a straight answer to my questions. Getter wouldn't tell me what his ghoul was up to at the time of the shooting and while Patrick did admit that he pulled the trigger, he would not tell me why. However, I was assured the body was cut up into tiny pieces and dumped into the ocean after a boat ride. Anyway, with uncooperative witnesses, I decided to put the case on an indefinite recess unless or until new information came to light.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Rusty</u></b><br /> <br /> Remember the ghoul who Spider found lurking outside Eve Liebsch's apartment the night EZE attacked? It turns out she is Patrick's ghoul. When we freed Patrick from a torpor encased in concrete, we did not arrange for him to woken up using potent vitae. Instead, we arranged with the almoner (Cooper) to have Patrick's blood ration delivered to his self storage container. As he is a neonate, we did not anticipate that this would take more than a few weeks.<br /> <br /> In addition, we brought a cot and sleeping bag for Rusty along with a cooler full of sandwiches, several gallon jugs of drinking water, a five-gallon toilet, and some paperback novels. She would be the one feeding him through a funnel after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Confession</u></b><br /> <br /> So, as I was walking away from the Jiffy-Lube where we were having our discussion, Patrick follows us.<br /> <br /> Patrick: &quot;Listen. I didn't want to say this in front of everyone in there... When I shot that guy, it was because he and another ghoul were getting ready to rape and kill one of your ghouls. The short one with dark hair. Well, when I was unable to take care of Rusty you treated her like she was one of your own. So, since I had the chance to return the favor, I did.&quot;<br /> <br /> I gave Patrick a long look before I left for home.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Home</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice has been spending a lot of time lately travelling around the city spying for the Mekhetocracy. The activities of Clan Nosferatu have her unhappy with her performance. I had to wait for her return near dawn before we could speak. The fact that I hadn't seen Mouse around the house for a past few days had not come as a surprise to me. She was after all on a mission to spy on our new neighbors.<br /> <br /> Well, Alice was not best pleased with this news. We were also disappointed with Mouse. Not because this happened to her, but because she did not tell us. Anyway, Alice invaded the mind of Mouse to view the events through the lens of her memories. Here is what happened.<br /> <br /> 1. Mouse decided one night to visit Tigger (Terry's Attendant) and planned to visit Elysium together.<br /> 2. As Mouse was just outside the haven of Terry and Kat (Alice's and my former haven) a van pulled up and she was pulled inside.<br /> 3. She was taken across bay to the quarantine zone to a secluded place quite a distance from the places where vampires normally gather.<br /> 4. As the two ghouls were discussing what they were going to do with her, Patrick showed up.<br /> 5. Patrick warned them to let her go, and when they didn't he shot one of them in the head.<br /> 6. The other ghoul fled.<br /> 7. Patrick and Rusty brought Mouse back and dropped her off across the street from our Haven.<br /> <br /> Before we went to sleep for the day, we took mouse into the bathroom and gave her a bath. Then we let her sleep with us for the day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Investigation</u></b><br /> <br /> With Alice back at my side, the investigation goes a bit faster from there. Here is what led to this ugly turn of events.<br /> <br /> 1. After the death of EZE, not all of his ghouls were found and disposed of. One of them escaped.<br /> 2. The surviving ghoul of EZE has been desperately trying to find a new regnant.<br /> 3. Charles Wood has not made any explicit offers to this survivor, but has mused many times in his presence about the poor treatment residents of the Quarantine Zone receive from the so called Citizens of Baltimore.<br /> <br /> <b>Charles Wood:</b> &quot;Wouldn't it be great if someone were to teach them a lesson? That there are consequences to their actions? What if someone were to just take one of their ghouls and kill it? Wouldn't that be great? I would have a lot of respect for whoever did that.&quot; (it seems to me that Mr. Wood is aware that he would be held responsible for the actions of this thralls. He was trying to manipulate the surviving ghoul without actually asking/ordering actions or offering compensation.)<br /> <br /> Well all this is well and good, but now we need to teach these little fucks a lesson.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Witness</u></b><br /> <br /> Alice and I felt that the lynchpin to this case is Getter's ghoul. He was an accomplice to the crime, but he did not get shot in the head. He wisely ran. Further, I am rather upset that the perpetrators tried to trick me into punishing the guy who rescued Mouse.<br /> <br /> So, the two of us go looking for Getter's attendant. After twisting Getter's arm, we discover that Charles Wood has forced him to hire Marco and Polo (discount mercenaries) to kill his ghoul. From there, we rush to the nearby docks. We have seen Marco and Polo operate there before.<br /> <br /> When we arrive, we find several bags of McDonald's hamburgers and discarded wrappers. The ghoul is eating his last meal (slowly) as Marco and Polo watch. We inform the two that we will be taking the ghoul. They are not happy with the prospect of having to give a refund, but we are able to intimidate the two and avoid violence. The ghoul spends a few days imprisoned in our basement while we make our plans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Courts</u></b><br /> <br /> Charles Wood wants to manipulate the courts? We will show him how to use the courts. We are going to chainsaw fuck him with the courts. After some legal advice from Anthony (reeve, invictus, my cousin) we decided to convince everyone who has been wronged in even the smallest degree to file a grievance against Charles Wood.<br /> <br /> 1. First, we spoke to Terry and Kat. Mouse was kidnapped right in front of their haven. Actions like these can lead other kindred to believe their haven is unsafe and therefore refuse invitations to visit, or refrain from inviting them to other events because they are too afraid to risk sending their own ghouls as couriers to their haven.<br /> <br /> Charles Wood is found guilty and sentenced to twenty-five lashes.<br /> <br /> 2. Soon after he received his lashes, Charles Wood received another summons to court. This time he is accused by Antony of the crime of travelling through his territory without permission and with bad intentions in his heart.<br /> <br /> Charles Wood is found guilty and sentenced to kill any and all ghouls he has, and is saddled with the responsibility of disposing of their bodies.<br /> <br /> 3. Soon after finishing that grim business, Charles Wood is summoned to appear in court once again. This time it is Alice and I who accuse him of the crime of kidnapping Mouse with the intent to do her harm. Charles Wood is found guilty. His sentence is that he will be banned forevermore from the creation of ghouls. In all of these cases, the ghoul of Getter is the star witness who is able to establish that Charles Wood is manipulating the late-former-ghoul of EZE into taking these actions.<br /> <br /> Lest you think that Alice and I have gone soft... at the conclusion of these legal proceedings we met with Antony in our official capacity as Marshals. We inform the Reeve that the vampire resident of the Quarantine Zone known as Charles Wood has failed his rabies test.<br /> <br /> Well we here in Baltimore do not simply exile rabid kindred to become a problem for some other domain. We kill them. And that is what we did to Charles Wood. Oh... and we returned Getter's ghoul to Marco and Polo. They have a contract to fulfill after all. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Heart to Heart</u></b><br /> <br /> Not long after, we found Miles (daeva, Carthian) looking sort of depressed standing by the water and decided to talk to him. Miles was feeling disappointed about the failed Jiffy-Lube-Elysium and embarrassment about the behavior of his fellow Quarantine Zone Residents. This is our home, and this is how they behave?&quot; He was also upset about the treatment they had been receiving from the Baltimore authorities.<br /> <br /> <b>Miles:</b> &quot;We chose to join you. We shouldn't be treated this way. We should be able to go wherever we want. Why are we treated like spies and threats. We chose Baltimore. We want to be part of Baltimore.&quot;<br /> <b>Alice:</b> &quot;Miles... Fairness seems to be something that is really important to you. Fine. You chose to join us, but we didn't choose you. isn't it only fair that we get to choose too?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":64,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","user":"figurehead","date":". 05-10-2015, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T04:03:21-07:00","id":509770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/437815-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-actual-play-part-7?p=509764#post509764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><u>The Courts</u></b><br /> <br /> Charles Wood wants to manipulate the courts? We will show him how to use the courts. We are going to chainsaw fuck him with the courts. After some legal advice from Anthony (reeve, invictus, my cousin) we decided to convince everyone who has been wronged in even the smallest degree to file a grievance against Charles Wood.<br /> <br /> 1. First, we spoke to Terry and Kat. Mouse was kidnapped right in front of their haven. Actions like these can lead other kindred to believe their haven is unsafe and therefore refuse invitations to visit, or refrain from inviting them to other events because they are too afraid to risk sending their own ghouls as couriers to their haven.<br /> <br /> Charles Wood is found guilty and sentenced to twenty-five lashes.<br /> <br /> 2. Soon after he received his lashes, Charles Wood received another summons to court. This time he is accused by Antony of the crime of travelling through his territory without permission and with bad intentions in his heart.<br /> <br /> Charles Wood is found guilty and sentenced to kill any and all ghouls he has, and is saddled with the responsibility of disposing of their bodies.<br /> <br /> 3. Soon after finishing that grim business, Charles Wood is summoned to appear in court once again. This time it is Alice and I who accuse him of the crime of kidnapping Mouse with the intent to do her harm. Charles Wood is found guilty. His sentence is that he will be banned forevermore from the creation of ghouls. In all of these cases, the ghoul of Getter is the star witness who is able to establish that Charles Wood is manipulating the late-former-ghoul of EZE into taking these actions.<br /> <br /> Lest you think that Alice and I have gone soft... at the conclusion of these legal proceedings we met with Antony in our official capacity as Marshals. We inform the Reeve that the vampire resident of the Quarantine Zone known as Charles Wood has failed his rabies test.<br /> <br /> Well we here in Baltimore do not simply exile rabid kindred to become a problem for some other domain. We kill them. And that is what we did to Charles Wood.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what was the purpose of the trials if you got him killed in the end anyways?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T05:12:12-07:00","id":509786,"title":"","content":"The purpose of the trials was to instill fear in the hearts of others who might think it's a wise idea to attack Alice, myself, or any of our friends/family/slaves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T04:12:56-07:00","id":510530,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Katherine and Fishie</u></b><br /> <br /> Katherine and Fishie were sired by the same vampire, a nomad. Though to call them sisters would be a mistake. Katherine's sire dropped Fishie on her doorstep a few years ago. Fishie was a disobedient pain in the ass and eventually Katherine kicked her out on her ass. She was apparently something of a pain to Roy (regent of territory to the NW of Baltimore) as he banished her from his territory.<br /> <br /> From there, Fishie drifted to the NE territory which was at the time controlled by &quot;the boss&quot; (lancea sanctum mobsters; allies of Septimus) who were in a power struggle is Pasha. Pasha had Fishie break into my haven and kidnap Felicity (my younger sister.)<br /> <br /> Felicity was saved. Pasha was killed in a duel. Fishie was made into a special project. We released her into the Quarantine Zone and made sure that her unlife was as unpleasant as we could, without actually getting her to rebel. Over time, we broke her spirit and left her living there as a pathetic creature. She is meant to be an unliving warning to others: If you fuck with us, we will ruin you. In all honesty, I can't even remember what her name was. Everyone calls her Fishie now, and she answers to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>At Fishie's Place</u></b><br /> <br /> So, one night Alice and I are hanging out in the Quarantine Zone under cover of Obfuscate. From a nearby rooftop, we notice that a few vampires are waiting outside the haven of Fishie. Those vampires are Hope, Karma, and Trenton (new Quarantine Zone residents.)<br /> <br /> There is a narrow staircase leading to Fishie's upstairs apartment. When the door opens, Katherine emerges and begins to walk down. Hope and Karma are blocking her way and Trenton is nearby watching.<br /> <br /> <b>Karma:</b> &quot;Who the fuck are you? and what are you doing in our territory?&quot;<br /> <b>Katherine:</b> &quot;Just leaving actually.&quot;<br /> <b>Karma:</b> &quot;I don't think so. You're not leaving until you've introduced yourself. I checked with Cooper and he says you're neither a Citizen nor a Resident and that makes you fair game.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alice and I move into position as the vampires continue to argue. Combat starts and Katherine wins initiative. Before anyone else can act, she quick draws a water bottle and squirts Karma with a clear liquid. My nose soon informs me that Karma is covered in lighter fluid. Everyone scatters and Katherine walks.<br /> <br /> Alice and I catch up to her on the bridge and have a short conversation. I suggest we leave before Karma is finished with her bath in the bay. On the other side of the bridge we enter Alice's and my territory. Katherine is asking what the fuck was the problem with those other vampires and wondering about travelling within Baltimore.<br /> <br /> Felix (obviously joking):&quot;Well, speaking of travel rights we are now standing on my territory.&quot;<br /> Katherine: &quot;Oh, will this suffice?&quot;<br /> <br /> Katherine reaches into her coat and pulls out an envelope, which she hands to me. Inside is a letter which bears her likeness in the engraved style one is accustomed to seeing on dollar bills. It reads something like this: &quot;By order of the Seneschal in the name of the Prince, the bearer of this note is to be afforded safe travel without hindrance through the His lands.&quot;<br /> <br /> I had been planning to escort Katherine through the Quarantine Zone and Kiddie Pool before letting her go on her merry way. After reading this letter, I ask her where she is headed and offer to escort her safely there. I also advise her that in the future, she should consider showing her writ of passage before trouble starts rather than after.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Big Trouble</u></b><br /> <br /> Well... Karma has really stepped in it. She has defied the orders of the Prince. The fact that she didn't know will be a mitigating factor insofar as it will prevent her from being executed. However, it is not her place to police the Quarantine Zone (as it happens that dubious honor rests with Alice and me.) I draft a summons and present it to Karma informing her that she will be standing trial in three nights. The summons is written in Latin, but that's her problem.<br /> <br /> So, three nights hence I arrive in the Quarantine Zone at the Jiffy-Lube. I have arranged for there to be extra tables and chairs for the trial I am about to conduct. Alice and I bring Aika and Aiko (daeva twins, our slaves) with us for added security.<br /> <br /> Karma has figured out that she needs to be here (there isn't really a good Latin word for Jiffy-Lube) and the place is packed. Because her offense was directly against the Prince I will not be conducting this trial in the casual way I usually do (ie: in English.)<br /> <br /> So, I call the trial to order in Latin and ask if Karma has used the three days lead time to procure a translator for herself. She looked pretty confused, but then Patrick stepped forward and asked (in Latin) if he could serve as translator. I then ask if she has procured for herself a lawyer. Miles is trying to get her to accept him as a councilor, but Karma insists that she can defend herself.<br /> <br /> One by one, I question my witnesses via the translator. Hope and Trenton both testify that Karma at no time took aggressive action toward Katherine (this trial would have been a lot more simple had Katherine not won initiative that night.) Finally, Karma herself took the stand, and swore that it was not her who started the fight that night.<br /> <br /> Next, we brought Katherine to the stand. She is our surprise witness. Katherine begins by stating that she does not know Latin. I tell her that she can testify in the vernacular, if she would like. She counters that she would be most comfortable to testify in French. I allow it. (way back at character creation I took the well travelled merit and several language merits to represent the time I spent travelling with my sire.)<br /> <br /> At the conclusion of Katherine's testimony, I announce a 15 min recess to think over the facts. When we return, I pronounce my judgment:<br /> <br /> <br /> Felix (in latin; Patrick translating):&quot;I have weighed the testimony of all the witnesses, and I have found the testimony of Katherine to be the most convincing...&quot;<br /> Karma: &quot;This is bullshit! That bitch is a liar!&quot;<br /> Karma stands and runs across the room at Katherine. Aika and Aiko intercept her in a celeritous blur. Karma spends the remainder of the trial bound and gagged.<br /> Felix (more Latin): &quot;There is another witness to the crime in this courtroom. And that witness is me. I was watching you all on the night in question, unseen. I know which of the witnesses here stretched the truth and which one's did not. I therefore find Karma guilty acting against the wishes of the Prince. Because Karma hindered the movement of Katherine your movement will be hindered. By order of the court: the vampire known as Karma will be hobbled by having her feet removed with a butchers cleaver. Further, for disrespecting the court with her words: the vampire known as Karma will have her tongue removed. Finally, for attempting to assault a witness in a court of the City of Baltimore: the vampire known as Karma will receive 10 lashes.&quot;<br /> <br /> After the trial, Karma screams that she wants to appeal. Karma's feet are spared pending appeal, but her lashes and tongue removal are carried out and we leave.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Mission: Possible</u></b><br /> <br /> About four days later, we are called to the office of Michael Seville. Once there, he begins by asking us a few questions about our competence with the discipline of Obfuscate. Specifically he wants to know if we have the ability to disguise ourselves as someone else. We do.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;Now before I tell you any of the specifics of this mission, you need to be aware of the risks. This is a potentially very dangerous mission. The consequences for failing this mission would be great and felt city wide.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alice and I look at each other and decide that yes, we will help in whatever way we can.<br /> <br /> Seville tells us that there is going to be a transaction in the near future between Katherine and someone from out of town. It is our job to impersonate a pair of ghouls and join Katherine during the transaction. However, we are not there to protect Katherine, but to protect the person from out of town with whom she is doing business.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;It would be better for the city if one of you were to die defending this person than for the out of towner to be harmed in any way.&quot;<br /> <br /> This sounds delightful. Well, Alice and I agree to help anyway. We are told that the transaction would be taking place &quot;soon&quot; and we should be prepared to leave at short notice. Further, we are told that the deal could take place:<br /> <br /> 1. The Serpent of the Seas - a decommissioned cargo ship docked near Alice's and my territory.<br /> 2. An alley behind &quot;the Private Eye&quot; - a strip club in the quarantine zone.<br /> 3. An alley a few blocks away from the bus station on the NE side.<br /> <br /> In the nights that followed our meeting with Seville, we staked out each of these locations. We used our magic powers to get keys to all the nearby buildings, stashed emergency bags, and even panted bicycles around the potential sites. We also practiced our obfuscaate disguises. We didn't need to appear as any specific person, but we did need our disguises to be consistent from scene to scene for the duration of the night.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Tonight's the Night</u></b><br /> <br /> Not long after our preparations were made, Spider visited us at our haven. This is not an uncommon event. When we let him in, Michael Seville was standing there instead. He apologized for entering our haven under false pretenses but explained the need for secrecy. He told us that the time had been set, and after filling us in on the details left.<br /> <br /> Alice and I put on our disguises and traveled by bicycle to a diner in downtown Baltimore. There, we met several ghouls. Some known to us, and others not.<br /> <br /> 1. Rusty (Patrick's ghoul)<br /> 2. Snow - Quarantine Zone ghoul (i'm not sure who her regnant is.)<br /> 3. Marco or Polo's ghoul (I don't know his name)<br /> 4. unknown ghoul<br /> <br /> Soon after, a minivan pulls up to the diner and we feel the pull of Majesty as Katherine invites us all into her van. (and she didn't even offer us candy or puppies. wtf?) Anyway, we drive and Katherine stops at a gas station. Once there, some of the ghouls start grumbling and asking when we are going to get paid. Katherine decides to appease us with a little cash up front. We are each given $1000. Snow, who looks emaciated, says she is going to grab something from inside the gas station. I decide it would be a good idea to follow her, but when I round the corner I don't see her inside the store. Instead, she is across the street buying drugs on the corner.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Katherine asks the remaining ghouls if they are armed. All but Rusty are armed with firearms. Alice speaks up: &quot;Guns are loud. We should play it safe and use melee weapons instead.&quot; As I return to the group, Katherine is once again using her Majesty to keep the ghouls under control as she disarms them.<br /> <br /> Katherine: &quot;Where is the other girl?&quot;<br /> Felix: &quot;Across the street buying drugs. I say we leave her.&quot;<br /> <br /> We all pile into the minivan and leave, minus Snow. Soon we arrive in the NE side, near the bus station. Katherine opens the back of the van and pulls out a duffel bag, which she hands to one of the ghouls. We walk toward the meeting place. As we are travelling we are approached by Ryan (gangrel, Ancilla, game warden of the NE.) The NE has been declared fallow and Ryan is there to keep it that way. However, when Katherine produces her Writ of Passage, Ryan leaves without asking any questions.<br /> <br /> Finally, we arrive at the meeting place and we wait. After about 40 minutes, two humans arrive: a boy and a girl in their early 20s. The mortals pass a duffel over to Katherine, which we soon learn is filled with cash. Katherine orders the ghoul to hand over our duffel. The girl opens the duffel and pulls out a ziplock bag filled with crystal meth. She looks at it, then lays it aside. She reaches in again and pulls out a bag filled with ecstasy pills. She looks at it, then lays it aside. This process is repeated about 15 more times before she pulls out a vial of black tar.<br /> <br /> She holds the vial up to the light and then tosses it over to her partner. He gives it a long look and then opens it and smells it. When the vial opens, the scent of vitae enters my nostrils.<br /> <br /> The boy then places a second duffel on the ground and opens it. It is filled with gold coins in plastic vacuum packs.<br /> <br /> <b>The Girl:</b> &quot;Can any of you tell us where you go this? If so, you can have this bag.&quot;<br /> Katherine says she doesn't know where it's from and she isn't interested in further deals.<br /> <br /> <b>The Boy:</b> &quot;If you change your mind, we will be at the Motel 6 on the corner of 5th and Main, room 3 for a few more days.<br /> <br /> Katherine brings us all back to the minivan (Majesty) and we leave. Once we are dropped off, Alice and I haul ass back to the NE side and the Motel 6. On the way there, we stop at a payphone and make a call to Michael Seville's ghoul. When we became Marshals for Seville, he put us in contact with one of his ghouls. The ghoul gave us some information about safehouses and feeding grounds we could tap if we were wounded in the line of duty. We tell him that we will need 24 hour protection of the Motel 6 for the next few days.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Vigil</u></b><br /> <br /> So, Alice and I spent a few hours patrolling the area when we noticed a group of three ghouls creeping through the small wooded area which separates the Motel 6 from the nearby highway. Alice confirms via Auspex that they are here to kill and rob the two mortals who we are here to protect. I won't bore you with the details, but Alice and I did bad things to them. One died, and the other two left badly wounded with their memories sanitized as well as a dominate compulsion to get rid of this body of their friend that they just killed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seville's agents arrive and get checked into the motel. They will watch things from here on out. We meet Seville and give him a full report of what went down. Seville wants us to find the source of the drug which smells like vitae. He wants us to find the product manufactury and report back to him. &quot;Do not engage. Do not be seen. Just find it and report back.&quot;<br /> <br /> Before we leave, I tell Seville that I must turn myself in for punishment. I have killed without permission and in so doing transgressed the laws.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;We don't really have time for this. Fine...&quot; He leaves the room and returns with Jerome James. James Speaks in latin and accuses us of the crime to which I have just confessed.<br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;De minimus non curat lex.&quot; (the law does not concern itself with trifles.)<br /> <br /> With that out of the way, we leave.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Needle in a Stack of Needles</u></b><br /> <br /> This turned out to be a rather long and winding investigation. I'll try to distill it into the salient points:<br /> <br /> 1. We spoke to Katherine to find out wtf was going on. Here is what she told us:<br /> a. She owed a boon to Trevor (we have encountered this dood a long time ago in Roy's territoy.)<br /> b. To repay the boon, Trevor wanted her to handle this deal for him. Something about these mortals spooked him and he wanted Ketherine to take the risk for him.<br /> c. Katherine visited her vampire sister Fishie to ask for contacts to get some muscle to bring with her. This is how all those crappy Quarantine Zone ghouls got hired.<br /> <br /> 2. We tracked down Trevor.<br /> a. Trevor was approached by mortals who wanted drugs. They offered him an obscene amount of money to get them one sample of every drug sold in Baltimore.<br /> b. The vitae drug was hardest to get. Only Shaman knows where to get it.<br /> c. While I was talking to Trevor, Alice was prowling the neighborhood skimming the minds of bartenders and bouncers.<br /> d. She found out that in order to find him, the boy/girl mortal pair from out of town went from bar to bar asking about &quot;drug dealers who look like vampires&quot; and &quot;drug dealers who tend to wind up making out with people a lot more attractive than them.&quot; Sounds like Trevor sucks at the masquerade.<br /> <br /> 3. We returned to the Quarantine Zone and spoke to Shaman about the product.<br /> a. He told us that ghouls in Council Territory use the drug to take the edge off when they haven't been fed in a while.<br /> b. He tells us that he gets it from a pair of vamps called Rabbit and Gangrene who live in council territory.<br /> c. According to Shaman: Rabbit is the dangerous one. It is even rumored that he has killed a vampire in the Council Elysium without being caught.<br /> <br /> 4. We spend some time staking out the Council Elysium<br /> a. As the council continues to lose ground to the werewolves their Elysium has been getting less popular.<br /> b. Eventually, we find Gangrene. He was kinda hard to miss (Nosferatu with huge size merit.)<br /> c. We follow him first to his haven. He sleeps in the basement of a preschool. he feeds on the children who wander down there by day. Sometimes he even lets himself be seen.<br /> d. Next, we follow him to an abandoned YMCA. Very slowly and very obfuscatedly we follow him to the swimming pool. It takes us about 30 minutes to catch up to him because the halls and floors are littered with broken glass and other detritus which makes it difficult to maintain obfuscate.<br /> <br /> When we finally arrive at the pool we are treated to the following tablaeu:<br /> <br /> The pool is drained. In the deep end there is a caged vampire hooked up to a drug lab. There is a blood drip into the vampire and a vitae drip out of it. The vitae is boiled on a hot plate and then mashed into powder. In the shallow end of the pool there is a wooden totem adorned with the skulls of animals. On his knees in front of the totem is a man of native american descent. He is covered in ritual scars and is wearing a respirator as he paints occult symbols on the floor of the pool with red paint (or blood.) In the corner of the room, there is an adolescent girl chained to a radiator. She appears to be about 13 years old and is nude and shaved bald. She is huddled over a small table with a scale as she fills and measures small glass vials with a rust colored powder. Alice later tells me that the man in the pool is definitely a werewolf.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf:</b> &quot;I can't work like this. Get me a fresh one!&quot;<br /> Gangrene leaves.<br /> <br /> So yeah... I'm pretty sure we have found the manufactury. Alice and I leave. As slowly and carefully as we had entered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Debreifing</u></b><br /> <br /> We returned to Seville and made our report.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;I will answer your questions if that is what you wish, but now is your last chance to walk away with nothing by my gratitude and the gratitude of the city. You'll sleep better if you do.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alice and I decide that sleep is overrated.<br /> <br /> <b>Seville:</b> &quot;The two you encountered while traveling with Katherine are human wizards from Philidelphia. The red powder is some kind of tainted version of something they need. Someone is trying to draw attention to Baltimore&quot;<br /> <br /> Seville tells us to do nothing about the drug lab at the YMCA. It is above our pay grade and will be dealt with by those more powerful than us. Gangrene however, we can deal with. And we do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Warnings</u></b><br /> <br /> Recent events have reminded me of a scene which actually took place months ago. Alice and I were looking for her grandsire, Peter. When we arrived at his office the Primogen were meeting and the door was open. We overheard a few words from Appollonia.<br /> <br /> <b>Appollonia:</b> &quot;Our city is threatened by external deadly foes. We must unite inside her or we'll crumble from within. I have told you. I have warned you. Let the squabble now begin.&quot;<br /> <br /> (yes, I know this is from Harry Potter.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Post Script</u></b><br /> <br /> Out of character, I was a bit surprised that this mission came to us via Michael Seville instead of via the Mekhetocracy. The ST told me a few meta-game things:<br /> <br /> 1. He made competing rolls for the mekhetocracy vs Michael Seville's intelligence network. Seville won.<br /> 2. The Prince is in fact heading toward torpor. Some nights he is more lucid than others. The Prince has certain devotions which link him to the city of Baltimore and allow him to better direct the limited resources of the Mekhetocracy. It's easy to get mekhet eyes on a problem when the Prince knows where you need to be. It's harder when the 12 remaining mekhet do not have that kind of direction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This should bring things up to date. Thanks for reading <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> Let me know what you think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T05:38:33-07:00","id":510562,"title":"","content":"Awesome write up! (as always)<br /> Keep them coming <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/640-bram_pc","name":"Bram_pc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T23:59:23-07:00","id":512664,"title":"","content":"External supernatural enemies and an upcoming power vaccum at the top. This could get really interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T07:28:11-07:00","id":624282,"title":"","content":"Hi all. Just want to drop by and mention that we picked the game back up. Played for the first time in a few months last Sunday. Assuming all goes according to plan, we should be playing every other week, and I will update the thread once or twice a m